1
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:57,350
Now, I know 
what you're thinking.

2
00:00:57,510 --> 00:01:00,890
"No! Thor's in a cage. 
How did this happen?"

3
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:02,810
Well, sometimes 
you have to get captured

4
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:04,730
just to get a straight answer 
out of somebody.

5
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:07,150
It's a long story,

6
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:09,190
but basically, 
I'm a bit of a hero.

7
00:01:10,650 --> 00:01:12,950
See, I spent some time 
on Earth...

8
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:14,570
fought some robots,

9
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,280
saved the planet 
a couple of times.

10
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,330
Then I went searching 
through the cosmos

11
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:21,460
for some magic, colorful 
Infinity Stone things.

12
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:24,750
Didn't find any.

13
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,130
That's when I came across

14
00:01:26,210 --> 00:01:28,960
a path of death 
and destruction...

15
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:31,840
which led me all the way here 
into this cage...

16
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:34,800
where I met you.

17
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:42,640
How much longer do you think 
we'll be here?

18
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:00,290
Thor, son of Odin.

19
00:02:00,910 --> 00:02:04,210
Surtur, son of a bitch.

20
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:05,290
You're still alive.

21
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:09,800
I thought my father killed you 
a half a million years ago.

22
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:11,590
I cannot die.

23
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:13,510
Not until 
I fulfill my destiny...

24
00:02:13,670 --> 00:02:15,930
and lay waste to your home.

25
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:17,590
It's funny 
you should mention that.

26
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,060
Because I've been having these 
terrible dreams of late.

27
00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:22,470
Asgard up in flames, 
falling to ruins.

28
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:23,850
And you, Surtur,

29
00:02:23,930 --> 00:02:25,440
are at the center 
of all of them.

30
00:02:25,730 --> 00:02:29,440
Then you have seen Ragnarok, 
the fall of Asgard.

31
00:02:29,610 --> 00:02:31,440
- The great prophecy... 
- Hang on.

32
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:34,320
Hang on.

33
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,110
I'll be back around shortly.

34
00:02:37,410 --> 00:02:40,240
I really feel like we were 
connecting there.

35
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:44,370
Okay, so Ragnarok.

36
00:02:44,450 --> 00:02:46,120
Tell me about that. 
Walk me through it.

37
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:48,290
My time has come.

38
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:51,590
When my crown is reunited 
with the Eternal Flame...

39
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:54,420
I shall be restored 
to my full might.

40
00:02:54,590 --> 00:02:56,840
I will tower 
over the mountains...

41
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:59,600
and bury my sword 
deep in Asgard's...

42
00:02:59,850 --> 00:03:02,310
Hang on. 
Give it a second.

43
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:03,770
I swear I'm not even moving.

44
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:05,390
It's just doing this on its own.

45
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:07,980
I'm really sorry.

46
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:09,860
Okay, so let me 
get this straight.

47
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:13,650
You're going to put your crown 
into the Eternal Flame...

48
00:03:13,820 --> 00:03:16,200
and then you'll suddenly grow 
as big as a house?

49
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,530
A mountain!

50
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:20,740
The Eternal Flame that Odin 
keeps locked away on Asgard?

51
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:23,330
Odin is not on Asgard.

52
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:27,540
And your absence has left 
the throne defenseless.

53
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:29,540
Okay, so where is it? 
This crown?

54
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:32,630
This is my crown, 
the source of my power.

55
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:34,630
That's a crown.

56
00:03:34,710 --> 00:03:36,510
I thought it was a big eyebrow.

57
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:37,840
It's a crown.

58
00:03:38,010 --> 00:03:41,510
Anyway, it sounds like all I 
have to do to stop Ragnarok...

59
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,390
is rip that thing off your head.

60
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:47,270
But Ragnarok has already begun.

61
00:03:47,430 --> 00:03:49,230
You cannot stop it.

62
00:03:58,950 --> 00:04:02,030
I am Asgard's doom, 
and so are you.

63
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:05,790
All will suffer, all will burn.

64
00:04:05,950 --> 00:04:07,660
That's intense.

65
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:09,670
To be honest, 
seeing you grow really big...

66
00:04:09,830 --> 00:04:12,330
and set fire to a planet 
would be quite the spectacle.

67
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:15,170
But it looks like I'm gonna 
have to choose option B...

68
00:04:15,340 --> 00:04:17,090
where I bust 
out of these chains...

69
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:19,010
knock that tiara off your head,

70
00:04:19,090 --> 00:04:21,090
and stash it away 
in Asgard's vault.

71
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:24,260
You cannot stop Ragnarok.

72
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:25,510
Why fight it?

73
00:04:25,890 --> 00:04:29,350
Because that's what heroes do.

74
00:04:34,310 --> 00:04:36,360
Wait, I'm sorry. 
I didn't time that right.

75
00:04:38,190 --> 00:04:39,530
And, now!

76
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:47,700
You have made 
a grave mistake, Odinson.

77
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:50,410
I make grave mistakes 
all the time.

78
00:04:52,370 --> 00:04:55,130
Everything seems to work out.

79
00:06:13,870 --> 00:06:15,500
Heimdall, I know 
it's been a while,

80
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:17,580
but I could really use 
a fast exit.

81
00:06:19,090 --> 00:06:20,500
Heimdall?

82
00:06:21,510 --> 00:06:23,380
Heimdall was an idiot.

83
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:25,510
This job should have 
made him rich.

84
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:27,930
Now, the job ain't easy...

85
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:29,890
but it does have its benefits.

86
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:32,430
The Bifrost gives me 
access to everything

87
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:34,430
the Nine Realms has to offer.

88
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:36,900
I mean it's all mine 
for the taking.

89
00:06:38,310 --> 00:06:39,560
Behold...

90
00:06:41,730 --> 00:06:42,900
my stuff.

91
00:06:45,070 --> 00:06:46,910
I'm particularly fond of these.

92
00:06:47,070 --> 00:06:50,620
I pulled them out of a place 
on Midgard called Texas.

93
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:53,830
I even named them. 
Des and Troy.

94
00:06:54,910 --> 00:06:57,040
You see, 
when you put them together...

95
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,080
they destroy.

96
00:07:18,350 --> 00:07:20,110
Heimdall, come on.

97
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:41,460
Stay!

98
00:07:43,210 --> 00:07:46,090
Heimdall? 
I'm running short on options.

99
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:48,840
<i>Heimdall?</i>

100
00:07:48,930 --> 00:07:50,340
Skurge?

101
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:55,100
Is that important?

102
00:08:02,110 --> 00:08:03,900
You girls are in for a treat.

103
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,410
Girls!

104
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:03,670
Well, well, well. 
Look who decided to pop in.

105
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,880
Thanks for scaring away 
my company

106
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:07,630
and drenching my workplace 
in brains.

107
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:08,920
Who are you?

108
00:09:09,010 --> 00:09:10,760
Don't you remember? 
I'm Skurge.

109
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:12,090
We fought together on Vanaheim.

110
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:14,470
Right. Where is Heimdall?

111
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:17,640
That traitor. No one knows. 
He's a fugitive of the throne.

112
00:09:18,310 --> 00:09:19,430
Traitor?

113
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:21,140
Yeah. Well, you see, 
Odin charged Heimdall

114
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:22,230
with negligence of duty...

115
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:24,270
but he disappeared 
before the trial.

116
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:25,560
Hard to catch a guy

117
00:09:25,650 --> 00:09:26,690
who can see 
everything in the universe.

118
00:09:26,730 --> 00:09:27,730
Sure.

119
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:30,360
Hold on. I'm supposed 
to announce your arrival.

120
00:09:54,550 --> 00:09:56,140
What the hell is that?

121
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:06,810
Brother. 
This is it.

122
00:10:07,110 --> 00:10:08,360
I take my leave.

123
00:10:09,230 --> 00:10:11,230
You fool, you didn't listen!

124
00:10:11,530 --> 00:10:12,530
I'm sorry.

125
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:13,740
Lady Sif, get help!

126
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:14,820
Somebody, help!

127
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:17,160
Sorry for all I've done.

128
00:10:17,410 --> 00:10:19,080
It's all right. Hold on.

129
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:22,660
I'm sorry I tried to rule Earth.

130
00:10:22,950 --> 00:10:24,160
They'd be lucky to have you.

131
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:27,170
I'm sorry about that thing 
with the Tesseract.

132
00:10:27,630 --> 00:10:29,170
- I just couldn't help myself. 
- I know.

133
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:30,500
I'm a trickster.

134
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,510
So mischievous.

135
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:35,380
Sorry about that time 
I turned you into a frog.

136
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:36,970
It was a wonderful joke.

137
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:39,260
'Twas indeed hilarious.

138
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:41,510
You are the savior of Asgard.

139
00:10:41,930 --> 00:10:43,850
- Tell my story. 
- I will.

140
00:10:43,930 --> 00:10:45,060
Build a statue for me.

141
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:46,940
We will build 
a big statue for you.

142
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:49,980
With my helmet on, 
with the big bendy horns.

143
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:53,110
I will tell Father 
what you did here today.

144
00:10:53,650 --> 00:10:54,940
I didn't do it for him.

145
00:10:55,990 --> 00:10:58,780
I didn't do it for him.

146
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:09,710
No!

147
00:11:13,420 --> 00:11:16,130
And so, 
Loki died of his wounds...

148
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:18,220
giving his life for ours.

149
00:11:18,510 --> 00:11:21,050
He fought back 
those disgusting elves...

150
00:11:21,350 --> 00:11:23,010
he brought peace to the realm.

151
00:11:23,310 --> 00:11:25,480
Loki, my boy...

152
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:27,940
'twas many moons ago I found you

153
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:29,980
on that frostbitten battlefield.

154
00:11:30,810 --> 00:11:33,230
On that day, 
I did not yet see in you...

155
00:11:33,530 --> 00:11:35,690
Asgard's savior. No.

156
00:11:35,990 --> 00:11:40,370
You were merely 
a little blue baby icicle...

157
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:44,370
that melted 
this old fool's heart.

158
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:49,330
Bravo! Bravo! 
Well done. Bravo.

159
00:11:54,090 --> 00:11:55,090
Father.

160
00:11:56,170 --> 00:11:57,170
Shit.

161
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,800
My son, Thor, has returned!

162
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:03,180
Greetings, my boy.

163
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:05,060
It's an interesting play. 
What's it called?

164
00:12:05,220 --> 00:12:07,180
<i>The Tragedy of Loki of Asgard.</i>

165
00:12:07,270 --> 00:12:09,190
The people wanted 
to commemorate him.

166
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:10,690
Indeed they should.

167
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:12,150
I like the statue.

168
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,730
A lot better looking than he 
was when he was alive, though.

169
00:12:14,770 --> 00:12:16,480
A little less weaselly, 
less greasy, maybe.

170
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:19,610
Do you know what this is?

171
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:23,490
The skull of Surtur. 
That's a formidable weapon!

172
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:25,450
Do me a favor. 
Lock this away in a vault...

173
00:12:25,490 --> 00:12:27,120
so it doesn't turn 
into a giant monster

174
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:28,580
and destroy the whole planet.

175
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:31,880
Thank you, dear.

176
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:34,630
So it's back to Midgard 
for you, is it?

177
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Nope.

178
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:39,130
I've been having this 
reoccurring dream lately.

179
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:42,090
Every night, 
I see Asgard fall into ruins.

180
00:12:42,390 --> 00:12:43,510
That's just a silly dream...

181
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:45,510
signs of an overactive 
imagination.

182
00:12:45,810 --> 00:12:46,810
Possibly.

183
00:12:46,890 --> 00:12:48,850
But then I decide to go 
out there and investigate.

184
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:50,140
And what do I find,

185
00:12:50,230 --> 00:12:52,980
but the Nine Realms 
completely in chaos.

186
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:56,110
Enemies of Asgard assembling, 
plotting our demise...

187
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,820
all while you, Odin,

188
00:12:57,900 --> 00:12:59,320
the protector 
of those Nine Realms...

189
00:12:59,490 --> 00:13:01,030
are sitting here 
in your bathrobe,

190
00:13:01,110 --> 00:13:02,110
eating grapes.

191
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:04,320
Yes, it is best to respect 
our neighbors' freedom.

192
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:07,580
Yes, of course, 
the freedom to be massacred.

193
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:11,540
Yes, besides I've been 
rather busy myself.

194
00:13:11,830 --> 00:13:12,830
Watching theater.

195
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:14,790
Board meetings, and security 
council meetings...

196
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,250
You're really gonna 
make me do it?

197
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:17,460
Do what?

198
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:23,180
You know that 
nothing will stop Mjolnir

199
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:24,760
as it returns to my hand.

200
00:13:25,050 --> 00:13:26,390
Not even your face.

201
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,770
You've gone quite mad. 
You'll be executed for this.

202
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:31,480
Then I'll see you 
on the other side, brother.

203
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:34,270
All right, I yield.

204
00:13:44,570 --> 00:13:45,570
Behold!

205
00:13:46,530 --> 00:13:47,620
Thor...

206
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:49,740
- Odinson. 
- No.

207
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:53,790
You had one job. Just the one.

208
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:56,960
Where's Odin?

209
00:13:57,250 --> 00:13:58,880
You just couldn't stay away, 
could you?

210
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,920
Everything was fine without you.

211
00:14:01,210 --> 00:14:03,760
Asgard was prospering. 
You've ruined everything.

212
00:14:04,130 --> 00:14:05,260
- Ask them. 
- Where's Father?

213
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:07,010
- Did you kill him? 
- You had what you wanted.

214
00:14:07,050 --> 00:14:08,560
You had the independence 
you asked for.

215
00:14:09,350 --> 00:14:11,430
Okay. I know exactly 
where he is.

216
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:25,700
I swear I left him right here.

217
00:14:27,370 --> 00:14:28,450
Right here on the sidewalk,

218
00:14:28,530 --> 00:14:30,120
or right there where the 
building is being demolished?

219
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,160
Great planning.

220
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:32,620
How was I supposed to know?

221
00:14:32,700 --> 00:14:34,370
Can't see into the future. 
I'm not a witch.

222
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:36,290
No? Then why do you dress 
like one?

223
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:38,670
- Hey. 
- I can't believe you're alive.

224
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,300
I saw you die.

225
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:42,090
I mourned you, I cried for you.

226
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:43,460
I'm honored.

227
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:44,840
Ask him.

228
00:14:45,010 --> 00:14:46,720
Hi. Would you mind taking 
a picture with us?

229
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:48,890
Sure.

230
00:14:48,970 --> 00:14:50,510
Start figuring out where he is.

231
00:14:51,470 --> 00:14:52,520
My God.

232
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,980
Sorry to hear 
that Jane dumped you.

233
00:14:54,810 --> 00:14:56,440
She didn't dump me, you know.

234
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:58,770
I dumped her. 
It was a mutual dumping.

235
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:02,730
What's this? 
What are you doing?

236
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:03,940
This isn't me.

237
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:09,660
Loki.

238
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:36,600
Thor Odinson.

239
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,700
God of Thunder.

240
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:51,280
You can put down the umbrella.

241
00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:11,090
So, Earth has, wizards now?

242
00:16:17,230 --> 00:16:18,390
The preferred term is

243
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:20,520
"Master of the Mystic Arts." 
You can leave that now.

244
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:22,860
All right, wizard.

245
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,230
Who are you? 
Why should I care?

246
00:16:24,770 --> 00:16:26,570
My name 
is Doctor Stephen Strange,

247
00:16:26,650 --> 00:16:28,610
and I have some questions 
for you.

248
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:29,700
Take a seat.

249
00:16:34,830 --> 00:16:35,830
Tea?

250
00:16:38,620 --> 00:16:39,620
I don't drink tea.

251
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,040
What do you drink?

252
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:42,500
Not tea.

253
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,590
So, I keep a watch list

254
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:49,510
of individuals and beings 
from other realms...

255
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,340
that may be a threat 
to this world.

256
00:16:51,430 --> 00:16:55,010
Your adopted brother, Loki, 
is one of those beings.

257
00:16:55,430 --> 00:16:57,680
He's a worthy inclusion.

258
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:01,100
Then why bring him here?

259
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:02,940
We're looking for my father.

260
00:17:03,350 --> 00:17:06,440
So, if I were to tell you 
where Odin was...

261
00:17:06,940 --> 00:17:09,110
all parties concerned would 
promptly return to Asgard?

262
00:17:09,490 --> 00:17:10,490
Promptly.

263
00:17:10,650 --> 00:17:11,860
Great! Then I'll help you.

264
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:14,280
If you knew where he was, 
why didn't you call me?

265
00:17:15,030 --> 00:17:16,200
I have to tell you, 
he was adamant

266
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,240
that he not be disturbed.

267
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:19,500
Your father said he had chosen 
to remain in exile.

268
00:17:20,790 --> 00:17:23,710
And you don't have a phone.

269
00:17:24,290 --> 00:17:25,790
No, I don't have a phone...

270
00:17:26,090 --> 00:17:27,750
but you could have sent 
an electronic letter.

271
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:28,880
It's called an email.

272
00:17:29,010 --> 00:17:30,840
- Yeah, do you have a computer? 
- No. What for?

273
00:17:31,130 --> 00:17:32,880
Anyway,

274
00:17:32,970 --> 00:17:34,550
my father is no longer in exile.

275
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,390
So if you could 
tell me where he is,

276
00:17:36,470 --> 00:17:37,470
I can take him home.

277
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:39,520
Gladly. He's in Norway.

278
00:17:40,350 --> 00:17:42,690
I'm just seeing 
whether this incantation

279
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:45,770
requires any Asgardian 
modifications.

280
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,480
Nope.

281
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:49,530
We don't need that.

282
00:17:55,570 --> 00:17:57,660
Will you stop doing that?

283
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,870
I need just one strand 
of your hair.

284
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:03,120
Let me explain something.

285
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:05,710
My hair is not to be 
meddled with.

286
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:14,720
We could have just walked.

287
00:18:17,720 --> 00:18:19,310
He's waiting for you.

288
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:20,680
All right.

289
00:18:20,970 --> 00:18:22,230
Don't forget your umbrella.

290
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:23,640
Yes.

291
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:32,440
Sorry.

292
00:18:35,150 --> 00:18:36,700
There we go.

293
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:39,700
I suppose I'll need 
my brother back.

294
00:18:40,330 --> 00:18:41,540
Yeah. Right.

295
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:50,090
I have been falling 
for 30 minutes!

296
00:18:51,090 --> 00:18:52,260
You can handle him from here.

297
00:18:53,010 --> 00:18:54,010
Yes. Of course.

298
00:18:54,130 --> 00:18:55,470
Thank you very much 
for your help.

299
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:56,680
Good luck.

300
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:58,720
Handle me? Who are you?

301
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:00,470
Loki.

302
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:02,100
You think you're 
some kind of sorcerer?

303
00:19:02,140 --> 00:19:03,930
Don't think for one minute, 
you second-rate...

304
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:04,980
Bye-bye.

305
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:31,380
Father?

306
00:19:33,210 --> 00:19:35,670
Look at this place. 
It's beautiful.

307
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:42,510
Father, it's us.

308
00:19:45,930 --> 00:19:47,440
My sons.

309
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:49,730
I've been waiting for you.

310
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:51,650
I know. We've come 
to take you home.

311
00:19:52,270 --> 00:19:53,480
Home, yes.

312
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,450
Your mother, she calls me.

313
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:00,990
Do you hear it?

314
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,660
Loki, lift your magic.

315
00:20:07,330 --> 00:20:09,830
Took me quite a while 
to break free from your spell.

316
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:11,500
Frigga would have been proud.

317
00:20:11,790 --> 00:20:14,300
Come and sit with me. 
I don't have much time.

318
00:20:21,180 --> 00:20:22,680
I know that we failed you.

319
00:20:23,010 --> 00:20:24,140
But we can make this right.

320
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:26,100
I failed you.

321
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:29,730
It is upon us. Ragnarok.

322
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:32,690
No, I've stopped Ragnarok. 
I put an end to Surtur.

323
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:34,480
No.

324
00:20:35,070 --> 00:20:37,030
It has already begun. 
She's coming.

325
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:40,400
My life was all that 
held her back.

326
00:20:40,490 --> 00:20:41,490
But my time has come.

327
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:46,160
I cannot keep her away 
any longer.

328
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:48,120
Father, who are you 
talking about?

329
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:51,790
Goddess of Death. Hela.

330
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,380
My firstborn.

331
00:20:55,590 --> 00:20:56,590
Your sister.

332
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:01,340
Your what?

333
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:06,640
Her violent appetites 
grew beyond my control.

334
00:21:07,930 --> 00:21:10,980
I couldn't stop her, 
so I imprisoned her.

335
00:21:11,060 --> 00:21:12,140
Locked her away.

336
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:16,400
She draws her strength 
from Asgard...

337
00:21:17,730 --> 00:21:21,240
and once she gets there, 
her powers will be limitless.

338
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:23,030
Whatever she is, 
we can stop her together.

339
00:21:23,070 --> 00:21:24,070
We can face her together.

340
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:25,320
No, we won't.

341
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:28,450
I'm on a different path now.

342
00:21:28,790 --> 00:21:30,080
This you must face alone.

343
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:34,210
I love you, my sons.

344
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:38,420
Look at that.

345
00:21:42,630 --> 00:21:44,180
Remember this place.

346
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:47,050
Home.

347
00:22:27,010 --> 00:22:28,050
Brother.

348
00:22:35,900 --> 00:22:38,480
This was your doing.

349
00:23:21,070 --> 00:23:22,270
So he's gone.

350
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:28,490
That's a shame. I would've 
liked to have seen that.

351
00:23:28,990 --> 00:23:30,410
You must be Hela.

352
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:33,330
I'm Thor, son of Odin.

353
00:23:33,740 --> 00:23:36,100
Really? 
You don't look like him.

354
00:23:37,540 --> 00:23:39,170
Perhaps we can come 
to an arrangement.

355
00:23:39,580 --> 00:23:41,210
You sound like him.

356
00:23:43,300 --> 00:23:44,300
Kneel.

357
00:23:44,710 --> 00:23:45,800
Beg your pardon?

358
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:51,640
Kneel.

359
00:23:55,140 --> 00:23:56,730
Before your queen.

360
00:23:58,140 --> 00:23:59,400
I don't think so.

361
00:24:10,110 --> 00:24:12,120
It's not possible.

362
00:24:13,280 --> 00:24:16,830
Darling, you have no idea 
what's possible.

363
00:24:37,140 --> 00:24:38,140
Bring us back!

364
00:24:38,230 --> 00:24:39,230
No!

365
00:24:48,400 --> 00:24:49,400
Loki!

366
00:25:36,580 --> 00:25:38,200
Who are you? 
What have you done with Thor?

367
00:25:43,370 --> 00:25:44,420
I'm Hela.

368
00:25:46,750 --> 00:25:48,300
I'm just a janitor.

369
00:25:49,840 --> 00:25:52,880
You look like a smart boy 
with good survival instincts.

370
00:25:55,970 --> 00:25:57,640
How would you like a job?

371
00:28:09,140 --> 00:28:10,600
Are you a fighter?

372
00:28:11,520 --> 00:28:12,770
Or are you food?

373
00:28:13,570 --> 00:28:14,940
I'm just passing through.

374
00:28:15,650 --> 00:28:16,940
It is food.

375
00:28:17,320 --> 00:28:18,320
On your knees.

376
00:29:01,030 --> 00:29:02,410
He's mine.

377
00:29:11,790 --> 00:29:12,790
Wait!

378
00:29:21,840 --> 00:29:22,840
Wait!

379
00:29:25,180 --> 00:29:26,180
He's mine.

380
00:29:26,430 --> 00:29:29,520
So if you want him, 
you go through me.

381
00:29:29,890 --> 00:29:31,140
But we've already got him.

382
00:29:33,020 --> 00:29:35,730
All right, then. 
I guess I go through you.

383
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:37,730
More food.

384
00:30:12,060 --> 00:30:14,440
Thank you.

385
00:30:49,810 --> 00:30:53,270
Scrapper 142. I need clearance 
and an audience with the boss.

386
00:30:53,850 --> 00:30:55,520
I've got something special.

387
00:30:55,810 --> 00:30:58,020
Hey! Where are you taking me?

388
00:30:59,570 --> 00:31:00,690
Answer me!

389
00:31:01,070 --> 00:31:02,150
Hey!

390
00:31:02,610 --> 00:31:04,990
I am Thor, son of Odin. 
I need to get back to Asgard.

391
00:31:06,150 --> 00:31:08,240
Many apologies, your majesty.

392
00:31:36,980 --> 00:31:40,520
It's come to my attention 
that you don't know who I am.

393
00:31:47,780 --> 00:31:51,200
I am Hela, Odin's firstborn...

394
00:31:51,330 --> 00:31:53,580
the commander 
of the Legions of Asgard...

395
00:31:53,870 --> 00:31:55,500
the rightful heir to the throne,

396
00:31:55,580 --> 00:31:57,120
and the Goddess of Death.

397
00:32:01,790 --> 00:32:04,300
My father is dead.

398
00:32:04,590 --> 00:32:06,340
As are the princes. 
You're welcome.

399
00:32:07,090 --> 00:32:08,430
We were once the seat

400
00:32:08,510 --> 00:32:10,390
of absolute power in the cosmos.

401
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:12,760
Our supremacy was unchallenged.

402
00:32:13,060 --> 00:32:16,020
Yet Odin stopped at Nine Realms.

403
00:32:16,310 --> 00:32:19,600
Our destiny is to rule over 
all others.

404
00:32:20,520 --> 00:32:23,570
And I am here 
to restore that power.

405
00:32:25,230 --> 00:32:26,740
Kneel before me...

406
00:32:26,860 --> 00:32:30,780
and rise into the ranks 
of my great conquest.

407
00:32:32,450 --> 00:32:34,120
Whoever you are...

408
00:32:34,330 --> 00:32:37,250
whatever you've done, 
surrender now!

409
00:32:37,540 --> 00:32:39,620
Or we will show you no mercy.

410
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:41,330
Whoever I am?

411
00:32:41,420 --> 00:32:44,000
Did you listen to a word I said?

412
00:32:44,290 --> 00:32:46,170
This is your last warning!

413
00:32:48,420 --> 00:32:50,510
I thought you'd be happy 
to see me.

414
00:32:56,220 --> 00:32:57,560
Fine.

415
00:33:10,950 --> 00:33:12,160
Charge!

416
00:34:06,330 --> 00:34:08,460
I've missed this.

417
00:34:08,550 --> 00:34:10,300
Still, it's a shame.

418
00:34:11,170 --> 00:34:13,260
Good soldiers dying 
for nothing...

419
00:34:13,340 --> 00:34:15,510
all because 
they couldn't see the future.

420
00:34:15,970 --> 00:34:17,220
Sad.

421
00:34:17,430 --> 00:34:20,430
Look, still alive.

422
00:34:28,110 --> 00:34:29,690
Change of heart?

423
00:34:30,110 --> 00:34:32,360
Go back to whatever cave 
you crept out of.

424
00:34:33,900 --> 00:34:35,110
You evil demoness!

425
00:34:39,160 --> 00:34:41,080
Let's go see my palace.

426
00:35:12,030 --> 00:35:14,280
<i>Fear not, for you are found.</i>

427
00:35:16,490 --> 00:35:18,320
<i>You are home, 
and there is no going back.</i>

428
00:35:21,410 --> 00:35:23,750
<i>No one leaves this place.</i>

429
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:25,620
<i>But what is this place?</i>

430
00:35:25,830 --> 00:35:28,920
<i>The answer is Sakaar.</i>

431
00:35:30,960 --> 00:35:33,050
<i>Surrounded by cosmic gateways...</i>

432
00:35:33,260 --> 00:35:35,970
<i>Sakaar lives on the edge 
of the known and unknown.</i>

433
00:35:36,300 --> 00:35:37,930
<i>It is the collection point</i>

434
00:35:38,010 --> 00:35:39,680
<i>for all lost 
and unloved things...</i>

435
00:35:40,010 --> 00:35:41,640
<i>like you.</i>

436
00:35:41,850 --> 00:35:44,470
<i>But here on Sakaar, 
you are significant.</i>

437
00:35:44,810 --> 00:35:46,180
<i>You are valuable.</i>

438
00:35:46,270 --> 00:35:47,890
<i>Here you are loved.</i>

439
00:35:47,980 --> 00:35:48,980
What the hell?

440
00:35:49,100 --> 00:35:52,150
<i>And no one loves you more 
than the Grandmaster.</i>

441
00:35:52,440 --> 00:35:54,400
<i>He is the original,</i>

442
00:35:54,480 --> 00:35:56,530
<i>the first lost 
and the first found...</i>

443
00:35:56,740 --> 00:35:57,820
<i>the creator of Sakaar...</i>

444
00:35:58,160 --> 00:36:01,200
<i>and father 
of the Contest of Champions.</i>

445
00:36:01,530 --> 00:36:05,660
<i>Where once you were nothing, 
now you are something.</i>

446
00:36:05,100 --> 00:36:09,040
<i>You are the property 
of the Grandmaster.</i>

447
00:36:09,420 --> 00:36:10,750
<i>Congratulations!</i>

448
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:14,340
<i>You will meet the Grandmaster 
in 5 seconds.</i>

449
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:16,050
<i>Prepare yourself.</i>

450
00:36:17,970 --> 00:36:19,090
<i>Prepare yourself.</i>

451
00:36:20,800 --> 00:36:24,010
<i>You are now meeting 
the Grandmaster.</i>

452
00:36:37,070 --> 00:36:39,200
He's wonderful. 
It is a he?

453
00:36:39,530 --> 00:36:40,700
It is a he.

454
00:36:40,780 --> 00:36:41,780
Yeah.

455
00:36:41,990 --> 00:36:43,950
I love when you come 
to visit, 142.

456
00:36:44,120 --> 00:36:45,620
You bring me the best stuff.

457
00:36:46,040 --> 00:36:47,700
Whenever we get 
to talking, Topaz,

458
00:36:47,790 --> 00:36:49,500
about Scrapper 142...

459
00:36:49,710 --> 00:36:51,080
what do I always say?

460
00:36:51,170 --> 00:36:53,130
"She is the..." 
And it starts with a "B."

461
00:36:53,340 --> 00:36:54,340
Trash.

462
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:57,090
No, not trash.

463
00:36:58,050 --> 00:36:59,550
Were you waiting 
just to call her that?

464
00:36:59,590 --> 00:37:00,970
It doesn't start with a "B."

465
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:02,260
Booze hag.

466
00:37:05,060 --> 00:37:07,270
I'm so sorry. No, "best." 
I was thinking about "best."

467
00:37:07,520 --> 00:37:08,930
'Cause I always say 
you're the best.

468
00:37:09,060 --> 00:37:10,810
She brought me my beloved 
champion, you know.

469
00:37:11,100 --> 00:37:12,810
You say that every time 
she's here.

470
00:37:13,060 --> 00:37:14,480
What have you brought today? 
Tell me.

471
00:37:14,560 --> 00:37:15,570
A contender.

472
00:37:15,770 --> 00:37:16,780
A what?

473
00:37:17,110 --> 00:37:19,070
I need to go closer. 
I want a closer look at this.

474
00:37:19,320 --> 00:37:21,110
Can you take us closer? 
Thank you.

475
00:37:33,710 --> 00:37:34,710
Pay this lady.

476
00:37:34,880 --> 00:37:36,500
Just wait a damn minute.

477
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:39,050
I'm not for sale.

478
00:37:45,510 --> 00:37:47,010
Man, he's a fighter.

479
00:37:47,220 --> 00:37:48,470
I take 10 million.

480
00:37:48,770 --> 00:37:49,770
Tell her she's dreaming.

481
00:37:49,980 --> 00:37:51,810
For heaven's sakes, 
transfer the units.

482
00:37:58,940 --> 00:38:00,400
You'll pay for this.

483
00:38:00,780 --> 00:38:01,990
No, I got paid for this.

484
00:38:03,990 --> 00:38:05,370
Here's what I wanna know.

485
00:38:07,160 --> 00:38:08,160
Who are you?

486
00:38:08,240 --> 00:38:12,210
I am the God of Thunder.

487
00:38:15,580 --> 00:38:16,790
I didn't hear any thunder,

488
00:38:16,880 --> 00:38:18,920
but out of your fingers, 
was that sparkles?

489
00:38:19,670 --> 00:38:21,260
What happened to my manners?

490
00:38:21,630 --> 00:38:23,090
I haven't 
properly introduced myself.

491
00:38:23,340 --> 00:38:25,140
Come on. Follow me.

492
00:38:25,590 --> 00:38:27,550
My name is Grandmaster.

493
00:38:27,760 --> 00:38:29,560
I preside over 
a little harlequinade

494
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:31,060
called the Contest of Champions.

495
00:38:31,430 --> 00:38:32,730
People come from far and wide

496
00:38:32,810 --> 00:38:34,100
to unwillingly 
participate in it.

497
00:38:34,390 --> 00:38:35,400
And you, my friend,

498
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:36,980
might just be part 
of the new cast.

499
00:38:37,150 --> 00:38:38,190
What do you say to that?

500
00:38:38,270 --> 00:38:40,440
We're not friends and I don't 
give a shit about your games.

501
00:38:40,480 --> 00:38:41,740
I'm going back to Asgard.

502
00:38:42,110 --> 00:38:44,200
Ass-gard.

503
00:38:44,990 --> 00:38:46,990
One, two, three, four.

504
00:38:48,660 --> 00:38:50,740
There was a wormhole 
in space and time beneath me.

505
00:38:50,950 --> 00:38:54,080
At that moment, I let go.

506
00:38:54,330 --> 00:38:55,330
Loki?

507
00:38:56,790 --> 00:38:58,380
Loki! Loki!

508
00:38:58,630 --> 00:39:01,880
Over here. Over here.

509
00:39:02,130 --> 00:39:03,340
- Excuse me one second. 
- Loki!

510
00:39:05,340 --> 00:39:06,510
- What? 
- You're alive?

511
00:39:06,590 --> 00:39:08,510
- Yes, of course I'm alive. 
- What are you doing here?

512
00:39:08,550 --> 00:39:09,600
What do you mean, 
what am I doing?

513
00:39:09,640 --> 00:39:10,680
I'm stuck in this stupid chair.

514
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:12,350
- Where's your chair? 
- I didn't get a chair.

515
00:39:12,390 --> 00:39:13,730
- Get me out of this one. 
- I can't.

516
00:39:13,770 --> 00:39:15,100
- Get me out. What? 
- I can't.

517
00:39:15,190 --> 00:39:16,230
I've made friends with this man.

518
00:39:16,270 --> 00:39:17,310
He's called the Grandmaster.

519
00:39:17,350 --> 00:39:18,730
- He's crazy! 
- I've gained his favor.

520
00:39:18,770 --> 00:39:20,400
The Bifrost brought me 
out here weeks ago.

521
00:39:20,520 --> 00:39:21,520
- Weeks ago? 
- Yes.

522
00:39:21,730 --> 00:39:22,730
I just got here.

523
00:39:22,980 --> 00:39:24,190
What are you whispering about?

524
00:39:25,280 --> 00:39:27,030
Time works real different 
around these parts.

525
00:39:27,200 --> 00:39:30,120
On any other world, I'd be, 
like, millions of years old.

526
00:39:30,410 --> 00:39:31,910
But here on Sakaar...

527
00:39:37,460 --> 00:39:40,000
In any case, you know this...

528
00:39:40,090 --> 00:39:41,420
You call yourself 
Lord of Thunder?

529
00:39:41,500 --> 00:39:43,880
God of Thunder. 
Tell him.

530
00:39:44,210 --> 00:39:45,760
I've never met this man 
in my life.

531
00:39:46,050 --> 00:39:47,550
- He's my brother. 
- Adopted.

532
00:39:47,630 --> 00:39:48,760
Is he any kind of a fighter?

533
00:39:49,090 --> 00:39:50,140
You take this thing

534
00:39:50,220 --> 00:39:51,430
out of my neck 
and I'll show you.

535
00:39:51,470 --> 00:39:53,060
Now, listen to that. 
He's threatening me.

536
00:39:53,310 --> 00:39:55,180
Hey, Sparkles, here's the deal.

537
00:39:55,480 --> 00:39:57,560
If you wanna get back 
to Ass-place, Assberg...

538
00:39:57,810 --> 00:39:58,900
Asgard.

539
00:39:58,980 --> 00:40:01,820
Any contender who defeats 
my champion...

540
00:40:02,020 --> 00:40:03,730
their freedom they shall win.

541
00:40:04,030 --> 00:40:05,570
Fine. Then point me 
in the direction

542
00:40:05,650 --> 00:40:07,110
of whoever's ass I have to kick!

543
00:40:07,450 --> 00:40:09,860
That's what I call, contender.

544
00:40:10,120 --> 00:40:12,410
Direction would be 
this way, Lord.

545
00:40:12,870 --> 00:40:14,080
Loki!

546
00:40:19,830 --> 00:40:21,960
Hey, hey, hey. 
Take it easy, man.

547
00:40:23,040 --> 00:40:24,750
Over here.

548
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:26,420
The pile of rocks 
waving at you. Here.

549
00:40:26,670 --> 00:40:29,130
Yeah, I'm actually a thing. 
I'm a being.

550
00:40:29,380 --> 00:40:31,010
Allow me to introduce myself. 
My name is Korg.

551
00:40:31,050 --> 00:40:32,470
I'm kind of like 
the leader in here.

552
00:40:32,640 --> 00:40:34,390
I'm made of rocks, 
as you can see.

553
00:40:34,470 --> 00:40:35,930
But don't let that 
intimidate you.

554
00:40:36,220 --> 00:40:37,390
You don't need to be afraid

555
00:40:37,480 --> 00:40:39,020
unless you're made of scissors.

556
00:40:39,230 --> 00:40:40,440
Just a little rock-paper-scissor

557
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:41,480
joke for you.

558
00:40:41,770 --> 00:40:44,400
This is my very good friend 
over here, Miek.

559
00:40:44,690 --> 00:40:47,320
He's an insect 
and has knives for hands.

560
00:40:48,070 --> 00:40:49,360
You're a Kronan, aren't you?

561
00:40:49,740 --> 00:40:52,200
- That I am. 
- How'd you end up in here?

562
00:40:52,450 --> 00:40:54,160
Well, I tried to start 
a revolution,

563
00:40:54,240 --> 00:40:55,540
but didn't print 
enough pamphlets.

564
00:40:55,580 --> 00:40:56,950
So hardly anyone turned up,

565
00:40:57,040 --> 00:40:59,620
except for my mum 
and her boyfriend, who I hate.

566
00:40:59,960 --> 00:41:01,250
As punishment, I was forced

567
00:41:01,330 --> 00:41:03,710
to be in here 
and become a gladiator.

568
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:05,460
Bit of a promotional disaster, 
that one.

569
00:41:05,550 --> 00:41:08,130
But I'm actually organizing 
another revolution.

570
00:41:08,420 --> 00:41:09,470
I don't know 
if you'd be interested

571
00:41:09,510 --> 00:41:10,550
in something like that.

572
00:41:10,630 --> 00:41:12,300
Do you reckon 
you'd be interested?

573
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:15,600
How did you...

574
00:41:15,850 --> 00:41:18,430
Yeah, no. 
This whole thing is a circle.

575
00:41:18,730 --> 00:41:21,770
But not a real circle, 
more like a freaky circle.

576
00:41:22,100 --> 00:41:23,270
This doesn't make any sense.

577
00:41:23,350 --> 00:41:24,690
No, nothing makes sense 
here, man.

578
00:41:24,900 --> 00:41:26,270
The only thing 
that does make sense

579
00:41:26,360 --> 00:41:27,730
is that nothing makes sense.

580
00:41:28,070 --> 00:41:30,280
Has anyone here fought 
the Grandmaster's champion?

581
00:41:30,570 --> 00:41:31,570
Doug has.

582
00:41:31,740 --> 00:41:32,740
Doug!

583
00:41:32,990 --> 00:41:33,990
Our luck, Doug's dead.

584
00:41:34,070 --> 00:41:35,070
That's right.

585
00:41:35,240 --> 00:41:36,330
Everyone who fights

586
00:41:36,410 --> 00:41:37,830
the Grandmaster's champion 
perishes.

587
00:41:37,950 --> 00:41:39,500
What about you? 
You're made of rocks.

588
00:41:39,750 --> 00:41:42,290
Perishable rock. There you go. 
Another one gone.

589
00:41:42,620 --> 00:41:44,380
Yeah, no, I just do 
the smaller fights,

590
00:41:44,460 --> 00:41:46,290
warm up the crowd and whatnot.

591
00:41:46,590 --> 00:41:48,210
Wait. You're not gonna 
face him, are you?

592
00:41:48,510 --> 00:41:49,800
Yes, I am.

593
00:41:50,130 --> 00:41:51,880
Gonna fight him, win,

594
00:41:51,970 --> 00:41:53,340
and get the hell out 
of this place.

595
00:41:54,010 --> 00:41:55,760
That's exactly 
what Doug used to say.

596
00:41:56,100 --> 00:41:57,810
See you later, new Doug.

597
00:42:07,730 --> 00:42:09,360
Does no one remember me?

598
00:42:10,150 --> 00:42:12,400
Has no one been taught 
our history?

599
00:42:18,200 --> 00:42:19,540
Look at these lies.

600
00:42:20,370 --> 00:42:21,700
Goblets and garden parties?

601
00:42:24,080 --> 00:42:25,630
Peace treaties?

602
00:42:26,540 --> 00:42:27,670
Odin...

603
00:42:27,920 --> 00:42:29,420
proud to have it...

604
00:42:29,710 --> 00:42:30,960
ashamed of how he got it.

605
00:42:50,400 --> 00:42:52,530
We were unstoppable.

606
00:42:52,610 --> 00:42:54,530
I was his weapon in the conquest

607
00:42:54,610 --> 00:42:57,070
that built Asgard's empire.

608
00:42:59,950 --> 00:43:03,250
One by one, 
the realms became ours.

609
00:43:03,500 --> 00:43:07,580
But then, simply because 
my ambition outgrew his...

610
00:43:07,880 --> 00:43:12,420
he banished me, caged me, 
locked me away like an animal.

611
00:43:12,800 --> 00:43:15,470
Before that, Asgard's warriors 
were honored...

612
00:43:15,760 --> 00:43:19,260
their bodies buried as heroes 
beneath this very palace.

613
00:43:30,520 --> 00:43:32,190
- Odin's treasures. 
- Fake.

614
00:43:34,490 --> 00:43:36,900
Most of the stuff in here 
is fake.

615
00:43:37,610 --> 00:43:38,700
Or weak.

616
00:43:40,910 --> 00:43:42,790
Smaller than I thought 
it would be.

617
00:43:43,950 --> 00:43:45,460
That's not bad.

618
00:43:45,540 --> 00:43:47,210
But this...

619
00:43:47,920 --> 00:43:49,920
The Eternal Flame.

620
00:44:18,360 --> 00:44:20,530
Want to see what true power 
really looks like?

621
00:44:49,390 --> 00:44:51,980
Fenris, my darling, 
what have they done to you?

622
00:44:54,520 --> 00:44:58,530
With the Eternal Flame, 
you are reborn.

623
00:45:14,210 --> 00:45:16,000
I've missed you.

624
00:45:16,960 --> 00:45:18,760
I've missed you all.

625
00:45:21,590 --> 00:45:22,590
Odin...

626
00:45:22,890 --> 00:45:26,060
I bid you take your place 
in the halls of Valhalla...

627
00:45:26,350 --> 00:45:28,600
where the brave 
shall live forever.

628
00:45:30,140 --> 00:45:32,400
Nor shall we mourn 
but rejoice...

629
00:45:32,770 --> 00:45:34,020
for those that have died...

630
00:45:34,110 --> 00:45:35,400
the glorious death.

631
00:45:43,490 --> 00:45:44,780
Hurts, doesn't it?

632
00:45:45,070 --> 00:45:46,080
Being lied to.

633
00:45:47,120 --> 00:45:48,450
Being told you're one thing

634
00:45:48,540 --> 00:45:50,410
and then learning 
it's all a fiction.

635
00:45:55,380 --> 00:45:57,500
You didn't think I'd really 
come and see you, did you?

636
00:45:57,550 --> 00:45:59,170
This place is disgusting.

637
00:46:02,180 --> 00:46:03,890
Does this mean 
you don't want my help?

638
00:46:04,180 --> 00:46:06,220
Look, I couldn't jeopardize my 
position with the Grandmaster.

639
00:46:06,260 --> 00:46:07,640
It took me time 
to win his trust.

640
00:46:07,720 --> 00:46:09,220
He's a lunatic, 
but he can be amenable.

641
00:46:09,520 --> 00:46:10,730
What I'm telling you is,

642
00:46:10,810 --> 00:46:12,600
you could join me 
at the Grandmaster's side.

643
00:46:12,850 --> 00:46:13,850
Perhaps, in time,

644
00:46:13,940 --> 00:46:17,400
an accident befalls 
the Grandmaster, and then...

645
00:46:23,450 --> 00:46:25,820
You're not seriously thinking 
of going back, are you?

646
00:46:28,410 --> 00:46:30,100
Our sister destroyed your hammer

647
00:46:31,080 --> 00:46:32,460
like a piece of glass.

648
00:46:33,540 --> 00:46:35,370
She's stronger than both of 
us. She's stronger than you.

649
00:46:35,420 --> 00:46:36,710
You don't stand a chance.

650
00:46:36,880 --> 00:46:39,050
Do you understand 
what I'm saying to you?

651
00:46:43,590 --> 00:46:44,590
Fine.

652
00:46:47,300 --> 00:46:49,760
I guess 
I'll just have to go it alone.

653
00:46:50,680 --> 00:46:51,680
Like I've always done.

654
00:46:54,810 --> 00:46:55,980
Would you say something?

655
00:46:58,770 --> 00:47:00,190
Say something!

656
00:47:01,440 --> 00:47:03,530
What would you like me to say?

657
00:47:04,030 --> 00:47:06,110
You faked your own death...

658
00:47:06,410 --> 00:47:08,910
you stole the throne, 
stripped Odin of his power...

659
00:47:09,160 --> 00:47:10,620
stranded him on Earth to die,

660
00:47:10,700 --> 00:47:12,330
releasing the Goddess of Death.

661
00:47:12,950 --> 00:47:14,160
Have I said enough or would 
you like me to go back

662
00:47:14,210 --> 00:47:16,120
further than the past two days?

663
00:47:17,830 --> 00:47:19,210
You know, I haven't seen this

664
00:47:19,290 --> 00:47:21,340
beloved champion he talks of...

665
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:23,510
but I've heard 
he is astonishingly savage.

666
00:47:24,300 --> 00:47:26,880
I've placed a large wager 
against you tomorrow.

667
00:47:28,260 --> 00:47:29,260
Don't let me down.

668
00:47:33,310 --> 00:47:34,730
Piss off, ghost!

669
00:47:37,310 --> 00:47:38,770
He's freaking gone.

670
00:47:47,200 --> 00:47:48,200
Yuck!

671
00:47:48,320 --> 00:47:50,410
There's still someone's hair 
and blood all over this.

672
00:47:50,700 --> 00:47:52,030
Guys, can you clean up 
the weapons

673
00:47:52,080 --> 00:47:53,290
once you finish your fight?

674
00:47:53,450 --> 00:47:54,450
Disgusting slobs.

675
00:47:55,710 --> 00:47:57,120
Thor...

676
00:47:57,620 --> 00:47:59,420
wanna use a big wooden fork?

677
00:47:59,790 --> 00:48:00,790
No.

678
00:48:00,920 --> 00:48:02,090
Yeah, not really useful.

679
00:48:02,300 --> 00:48:04,010
Unless you're fighting off 
three vampires

680
00:48:04,090 --> 00:48:05,670
that were huddled together.

681
00:48:06,670 --> 00:48:08,130
I really wish I had my hammer.

682
00:48:08,550 --> 00:48:09,550
Hammer?

683
00:48:09,760 --> 00:48:11,260
Quite unique. 
It was made from this

684
00:48:11,350 --> 00:48:13,310
special metal from the heart 
of a dying star.

685
00:48:13,890 --> 00:48:15,390
And when I spun it really, 
really fast,

686
00:48:15,430 --> 00:48:16,930
it gave me the ability to fly.

687
00:48:17,060 --> 00:48:18,060
You rode a hammer?

688
00:48:18,310 --> 00:48:19,730
No, I didn't ride the hammer.

689
00:48:20,150 --> 00:48:21,440
The hammer rode you 
on your back?

690
00:48:21,560 --> 00:48:23,150
No. I used to spin it 
really fast,

691
00:48:23,230 --> 00:48:24,820
and it would pull me off the...

692
00:48:24,900 --> 00:48:26,990
My God. 
A hammer pulled you off?

693
00:48:27,070 --> 00:48:28,820
The ground. It would pull me 
off the ground,

694
00:48:28,910 --> 00:48:30,700
up into the air, 
and I would fly.

695
00:48:30,990 --> 00:48:31,990
Every time I threw it,

696
00:48:32,070 --> 00:48:33,870
it would always come back to me.

697
00:48:34,240 --> 00:48:35,410
Sounds like you had 
a pretty special

698
00:48:35,450 --> 00:48:36,870
and intimate relationship 
with this hammer...

699
00:48:36,910 --> 00:48:38,040
and that losing it

700
00:48:38,120 --> 00:48:39,920
was almost comparable 
to losing a loved one.

701
00:48:41,040 --> 00:48:43,130
That's a nice way of putting it.

702
00:48:44,800 --> 00:48:46,050
I said they're mine.

703
00:48:47,590 --> 00:48:49,470
See her, that's the one 
that put me in here.

704
00:48:49,800 --> 00:48:52,010
Yeah. Scrapper 142.

705
00:48:52,090 --> 00:48:54,220
Gotta watch out 
for those Asgardians, man.

706
00:48:54,310 --> 00:48:55,890
They are hard to perish.

707
00:48:56,100 --> 00:48:57,480
Asgardian?

708
00:48:59,310 --> 00:49:01,190
Hey. Hey.

709
00:49:01,940 --> 00:49:02,940
Hey.

710
00:49:03,310 --> 00:49:05,940
Do not zap me with that thing. 
I just wanna talk.

711
00:49:07,650 --> 00:49:09,030
Asgard is in danger.

712
00:49:13,530 --> 00:49:14,990
My God, you're a Valkyrie.

713
00:49:16,080 --> 00:49:18,290
I used to wanna be a Valkyrie 
when I was younger...

714
00:49:18,620 --> 00:49:20,920
until I found out that 
you were all women.

715
00:49:21,080 --> 00:49:22,120
There's nothing wrong 
with women, of course.

716
00:49:22,170 --> 00:49:23,170
I love women.

717
00:49:23,380 --> 00:49:24,790
Sometimes a little too much.

718
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:26,050
Not in a creepy way,

719
00:49:26,130 --> 00:49:27,840
just more 
of a respectful appreciation.

720
00:49:28,130 --> 00:49:29,420
I think it's great that there is

721
00:49:29,470 --> 00:49:32,510
an elite force 
of women warriors.

722
00:49:32,760 --> 00:49:34,180
It's about time.

723
00:49:35,680 --> 00:49:36,810
Are you done?

724
00:49:36,890 --> 00:49:37,930
Lord of Thunder, you're up.

725
00:49:37,970 --> 00:49:39,100
Please, help me. 
I need your help.

726
00:49:39,140 --> 00:49:40,140
Bye.

727
00:49:40,230 --> 00:49:42,400
Fine, then you must be 
a traitor or a coward.

728
00:49:42,690 --> 00:49:44,940
Because the Valkyrie is sworn 
to protect the throne.

729
00:49:45,560 --> 00:49:48,730
Listen closely, your majesty. 
This is Sakaar, not Asgard.

730
00:49:49,360 --> 00:49:50,950
And I'm a Scrapper, 
not a Valkyrie.

731
00:49:54,280 --> 00:49:56,160
Bring him in for processing.

732
00:49:56,530 --> 00:50:00,250
And no one escapes this place. 
So you're gonna die anyway.

733
00:50:12,170 --> 00:50:13,630
Now, don't you move.

734
00:50:14,010 --> 00:50:16,510
My hands ain't as steady 
as they used to be.

735
00:50:16,760 --> 00:50:19,560
By Odin's beard, 
you shall not cut my hair...

736
00:50:19,890 --> 00:50:22,350
lest you feel the wrath 
of the mighty Thor.

737
00:50:26,730 --> 00:50:29,110
Please. Please, kind sir, 
do not cut my hair.

738
00:50:30,440 --> 00:50:31,780
Please! No!

739
00:50:31,990 --> 00:50:33,030
No!

740
00:50:45,330 --> 00:50:48,090
<i>Look at all of you.</i>

741
00:50:48,170 --> 00:50:49,840
<i>What a show! What a night!</i>

742
00:50:50,090 --> 00:50:51,090
<i>Who's having fun?</i>

743
00:50:52,010 --> 00:50:53,880
<i>Please, I'm your host.</i>

744
00:50:54,130 --> 00:50:55,300
<i>Big round of applause</i>

745
00:50:55,380 --> 00:50:57,260
<i>for all of our 
undercard competitors...</i>

746
00:50:57,510 --> 00:51:00,220
<i>who today died so gruesomely.</i>

747
00:51:00,470 --> 00:51:01,600
<i>Good sports.</i>

748
00:51:01,850 --> 00:51:03,430
<i>What a show! What a night!</i>

749
00:51:04,140 --> 00:51:07,770
<i>This is what you've come for, 
and so have I.</i>

750
00:51:13,820 --> 00:51:16,660
<i>And now, without further ado...</i>

751
00:51:16,740 --> 00:51:19,240
<i>it's main event time.</i>

752
00:51:21,160 --> 00:51:22,620
<i>Making his first appearance,</i>

753
00:51:22,700 --> 00:51:24,250
<i>though he looks 
quite promising...</i>

754
00:51:24,710 --> 00:51:26,370
<i>got a couple of tricks 
up his sleeve.</i>

755
00:51:26,870 --> 00:51:29,420
<i>I'll say no more, 
see what you think.</i>

756
00:51:29,920 --> 00:51:31,300
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, 
I give you...</i>

757
00:51:32,210 --> 00:51:34,380
<i>Lord of Thunder.</i>

758
00:51:57,700 --> 00:51:59,870
<i>Watch out for his fingers. 
They make sparks.</i>

759
00:51:59,950 --> 00:52:01,280
<i>Okay, this is it.</i>

760
00:52:01,780 --> 00:52:04,700
<i>Let's get ready to welcome 
this guy. Here he comes.</i>

761
00:52:13,840 --> 00:52:15,130
<i>He is a creature.</i>

762
00:52:15,340 --> 00:52:16,630
<i>What can we say about him?</i>

763
00:52:16,720 --> 00:52:19,180
<i>Well, he's unique. 
There's none like him.</i>

764
00:52:19,430 --> 00:52:21,850
<i>I feel a special connection 
with him.</i>

765
00:52:23,680 --> 00:52:24,850
<i>He's undefeated.</i>

766
00:52:26,310 --> 00:52:27,730
<i>He's the reigning.</i>

767
00:52:30,150 --> 00:52:32,190
<i>He's the defending.</i>

768
00:52:32,690 --> 00:52:33,690
<i>Ladies and gentlemen...</i>

769
00:52:34,110 --> 00:52:35,110
<i>I give you...</i>

770
00:52:39,990 --> 00:52:43,660
<i>your Incredible...</i>

771
00:52:47,500 --> 00:52:49,330
Hulk!

772
00:52:49,960 --> 00:52:51,290
Yes!

773
00:52:55,250 --> 00:52:57,090
I have to get off this planet.

774
00:52:57,840 --> 00:52:59,590
Hey, hey, hey. 
Where you going?

775
00:53:07,980 --> 00:53:09,100
Hey!

776
00:53:09,810 --> 00:53:11,020
We know each other.

777
00:53:11,480 --> 00:53:13,360
He's a friend from work.

778
00:53:22,740 --> 00:53:24,280
Where have you been?

779
00:53:24,490 --> 00:53:26,490
Everybody thought you were dead.

780
00:53:26,790 --> 00:53:28,580
But so much has happened 
since I last saw you.

781
00:53:29,200 --> 00:53:30,750
I lost my hammer.

782
00:53:30,920 --> 00:53:33,880
Like, yesterday, 
so that's still pretty fresh.

783
00:53:34,420 --> 00:53:36,590
Loki. Loki's alive. 
Can you believe it?

784
00:53:36,880 --> 00:53:37,920
He's up there.

785
00:53:38,130 --> 00:53:40,050
Loki! Look who it is!

786
00:53:42,300 --> 00:53:44,300
Banner, I never thought 
I would say this...

787
00:53:44,390 --> 00:53:46,640
but I'm happy to see you.

788
00:53:46,970 --> 00:53:49,310
Hulk! Hulk! Hulk!

789
00:53:55,110 --> 00:53:56,110
Banner.

790
00:53:57,230 --> 00:53:58,480
Hey, Banner!

791
00:53:59,070 --> 00:54:01,070
No Banner. Only Hulk.

792
00:54:01,570 --> 00:54:02,610
What are you doing?

793
00:54:02,700 --> 00:54:04,570
It's me. It's Thor!

794
00:54:25,090 --> 00:54:26,260
Banner, we're friends.

795
00:54:26,350 --> 00:54:28,310
This is crazy. 
I don't want to hurt you!

796
00:54:35,440 --> 00:54:37,270
Here we go.

797
00:54:56,130 --> 00:54:57,210
What?

798
00:55:07,760 --> 00:55:09,140
Hey, big guy.

799
00:55:11,100 --> 00:55:12,980
The sun's getting real low.

800
00:55:24,280 --> 00:55:26,610
That's it. 
The sun's going down.

801
00:55:29,740 --> 00:55:31,330
I won't hurt you anymore.

802
00:55:31,740 --> 00:55:32,100
No one will.

803
00:55:45,170 --> 00:55:47,180
Yes! That's how it feels!

804
00:55:48,760 --> 00:55:50,300
I'm just a huge fan 
of the sport.

805
00:55:58,100 --> 00:56:00,440
All right. Screw it.

806
00:56:12,200 --> 00:56:13,330
I know you're in there, Banner.

807
00:56:13,370 --> 00:56:14,370
I'll get you out!

808
00:56:23,750 --> 00:56:25,760
What's the matter with you? 
You're embarrassing me!

809
00:56:25,840 --> 00:56:26,970
I told them we were friends!

810
00:57:58,470 --> 00:58:01,310
Thunder! Thunder! Thunder!

811
00:58:03,100 --> 00:58:07,900
Thunder! Thunder! Thunder!

812
00:58:39,560 --> 00:58:42,180
Another day, another Doug.

813
00:58:51,440 --> 00:58:53,360
What is that noise?

814
00:58:53,610 --> 00:58:56,280
The common folk aren't exactly 
falling in line.

815
00:58:56,780 --> 00:59:00,370
There's a resistance trying 
to knock down the front gates.

816
00:59:05,920 --> 00:59:07,670
Tell me about yourself, Skurge.

817
00:59:08,170 --> 00:59:10,380
Well, me dad was a stonemason. 
Me mum was...

818
00:59:10,630 --> 00:59:12,550
Right, yeah, 
I'll just stop you there.

819
00:59:12,630 --> 00:59:14,380
What I meant was...

820
00:59:14,880 --> 00:59:16,180
what's your ambition?

821
00:59:17,470 --> 00:59:20,720
I just want a chance 
to prove myself.

822
00:59:21,470 --> 00:59:22,470
Recognition.

823
00:59:22,850 --> 00:59:24,100
When I was young...

824
00:59:24,520 --> 00:59:28,020
every great king 
had an executioner.

825
00:59:28,310 --> 00:59:30,230
Not just to execute people...

826
00:59:30,520 --> 00:59:32,990
but also 
to execute their vision.

827
00:59:34,110 --> 00:59:36,780
But mainly to execute people.

828
00:59:37,070 --> 00:59:38,990
Still, it was a great honor.

829
00:59:40,950 --> 00:59:43,540
I was Odin's executioner.

830
00:59:44,830 --> 00:59:48,920
And you shall be my executioner.

831
00:59:54,550 --> 00:59:56,430
Let's begin our conquest.

832
01:00:07,940 --> 01:00:09,350
Skurge, where's the sword?

833
01:00:14,780 --> 01:00:18,490
That sword is the key 
to opening the Bifrost.

834
01:00:19,070 --> 01:00:20,450
Those people you mentioned,

835
01:00:20,530 --> 01:00:22,530
the ones who aren't 
falling into line...

836
01:00:23,200 --> 01:00:24,290
round them up.

837
01:00:48,230 --> 01:00:49,640
Excuse me.

838
01:01:01,740 --> 01:01:03,160
Sorry about that.

839
01:01:03,240 --> 01:01:04,620
These bloody things 
are everywhere.

840
01:01:05,990 --> 01:01:06,100
Come on.

841
01:01:41,950 --> 01:01:43,530
You'll be safe here.

842
01:02:53,020 --> 01:02:54,020
Are we cool?

843
01:02:57,900 --> 01:02:59,320
It's Hulk in a hot tub.

844
01:03:00,820 --> 01:03:02,240
So how long 
have you been like that?

845
01:03:02,860 --> 01:03:03,900
Like what?

846
01:03:04,530 --> 01:03:07,820
Like this. Big, and green, 
and stupid.

847
01:03:09,200 --> 01:03:11,120
Hulk always Hulk.

848
01:03:16,120 --> 01:03:17,290
How'd you get here?

849
01:03:18,210 --> 01:03:19,210
Winning.

850
01:03:19,290 --> 01:03:20,880
You mean cheating?

851
01:03:20,960 --> 01:03:23,300
Were they wearing one of these 
when you won?

852
01:03:23,550 --> 01:03:24,720
How'd you arrive here?

853
01:03:27,720 --> 01:03:28,720
Quinjet.

854
01:03:29,100 --> 01:03:31,430
Yes. Now, 
where is the Quinjet now?

855
01:03:36,390 --> 01:03:38,270
That's naked.

856
01:03:38,520 --> 01:03:41,150
He's very naked.

857
01:03:44,030 --> 01:03:45,950
It's in my brain now.

858
01:03:46,780 --> 01:03:47,780
Quinjet.

859
01:03:58,710 --> 01:03:59,790
Yes!

860
01:04:00,170 --> 01:04:01,420
I'm getting us out of here.

861
01:04:01,800 --> 01:04:04,050
This is a terrible, awful place.

862
01:04:04,300 --> 01:04:07,930
You're gonna love Asgard. 
It's big. It's golden. Shiny.

863
01:04:08,220 --> 01:04:09,470
Hulk stay.

864
01:04:09,800 --> 01:04:13,010
No, no, no. My people need me 
to get back to Asgard.

865
01:04:13,890 --> 01:04:15,560
We must prevent Ragnarok.

866
01:04:15,890 --> 01:04:16,980
Ragnarok?

867
01:04:17,390 --> 01:04:18,850
The prophesied death 
of my home world.

868
01:04:18,940 --> 01:04:20,310
The end of days, 
it's the end of...

869
01:04:22,690 --> 01:04:24,650
If you help me 
get back to Asgard...

870
01:04:24,940 --> 01:04:26,900
I can help you 
get back to Earth.

871
01:04:27,200 --> 01:04:28,200
Earth hate Hulk.

872
01:04:28,490 --> 01:04:29,820
Earth loves Hulk. 
They love you.

873
01:04:30,200 --> 01:04:31,410
You're one of the Avengers.

874
01:04:31,490 --> 01:04:32,910
One of the team, 
one of our friends.

875
01:04:33,330 --> 01:04:35,250
This is what friends do. 
They support each other.

876
01:04:35,450 --> 01:04:36,540
You're Banner's friend.

877
01:04:36,830 --> 01:04:38,870
I'm not Banner's friend. 
I prefer you.

878
01:04:39,210 --> 01:04:40,210
Banner's friend.

879
01:04:40,290 --> 01:04:41,290
I don't even like Banner.

880
01:04:41,420 --> 01:04:44,210
"I'm into numbers and science 
and stuff."

881
01:04:44,750 --> 01:04:46,170
Thor go. Hulk stay.

882
01:04:46,590 --> 01:04:47,590
Fine.

883
01:04:48,170 --> 01:04:49,180
Stay here.

884
01:04:50,050 --> 01:04:52,390
Stupid place. 
It's hideous, by the way.

885
01:04:52,680 --> 01:04:56,020
The red, the white. 
Just pick a color. Ridiculous.

886
01:04:56,980 --> 01:04:58,060
Smash you.

887
01:04:58,350 --> 01:05:00,520
You didn't smash anything. 
I won that fight.

888
01:05:00,810 --> 01:05:02,810
- I smashed you. 
- Yeah, sure, sure.

889
01:05:03,110 --> 01:05:04,730
- Baby arms. 
- What?

890
01:05:05,030 --> 01:05:06,190
Baby.

891
01:05:06,280 --> 01:05:07,690
Moron! You big child.

892
01:05:07,990 --> 01:05:09,070
Thor go!

893
01:05:09,150 --> 01:05:10,910
I am going.

894
01:05:15,040 --> 01:05:16,290
Thor go again.

895
01:05:21,170 --> 01:05:22,330
Thor home.

896
01:05:32,590 --> 01:05:33,930
Hulk trains.

897
01:05:34,350 --> 01:05:36,180
That's great. Have fun.

898
01:05:36,560 --> 01:05:38,100
- Hey, big guy. 
- Angry girl.

899
01:05:38,220 --> 01:05:39,390
What have you been up to?

900
01:05:39,730 --> 01:05:40,730
Winning.

901
01:05:51,240 --> 01:05:54,320
Heimdall, I know you can see me.

902
01:05:55,740 --> 01:05:57,450
<i>I need you to help me.</i>

903
01:05:59,910 --> 01:06:00,910
Help me see.

904
01:06:11,420 --> 01:06:13,760
I see you, but you're far away.

905
01:06:14,840 --> 01:06:15,890
What's going on here?

906
01:06:16,220 --> 01:06:17,510
Come see for yourself.

907
01:06:20,270 --> 01:06:21,730
I'm providing refuge 
in a stronghold

908
01:06:21,810 --> 01:06:22,810
built by our ancestors.

909
01:06:23,310 --> 01:06:26,560
But if the garrison falls, 
our only escape is Bifrost.

910
01:06:26,860 --> 01:06:28,780
You're talking 
about evacuating Asgard?

911
01:06:31,950 --> 01:06:33,860
We won't last long if we stay.

912
01:06:34,530 --> 01:06:35,870
She draws her power from Asgard

913
01:06:35,950 --> 01:06:37,120
and grows stronger every day.

914
01:06:37,370 --> 01:06:38,370
Come on.

915
01:06:42,460 --> 01:06:43,830
Hela is ravenous.

916
01:06:44,120 --> 01:06:45,130
If I let her leave,

917
01:06:45,210 --> 01:06:47,000
she'll consume Nine Realms 
and all the cosmos.

918
01:06:47,340 --> 01:06:48,340
We need you.

919
01:06:48,420 --> 01:06:49,550
I'm working on it. 
But I don't even know

920
01:06:49,590 --> 01:06:50,590
where the hell I am.

921
01:06:51,130 --> 01:06:53,430
You're on a planet surrounded 
by doorways. Go through one.

922
01:06:53,470 --> 01:06:55,260
- Which one? 
- The big one.

923
01:07:24,330 --> 01:07:25,500
Thor sad.

924
01:07:25,960 --> 01:07:27,040
Shut up.

925
01:07:29,420 --> 01:07:30,880
Thor sad.

926
01:07:32,130 --> 01:07:33,760
I'm not sad, you idiot.

927
01:07:34,260 --> 01:07:35,880
I'm pissed off!

928
01:07:37,050 --> 01:07:39,510
Angry. I lost my father.

929
01:07:40,760 --> 01:07:43,220
I lost my hammer.

930
01:07:43,350 --> 01:07:44,980
- You're not even listening. 
- Whining and crying.

931
01:07:45,020 --> 01:07:46,190
Cry like baby.

932
01:07:46,600 --> 01:07:48,060
Don't kick stuff.

933
01:07:49,480 --> 01:07:51,520
You're being 
a really bad friend.

934
01:07:51,820 --> 01:07:52,820
You bad friend!

935
01:07:53,190 --> 01:07:54,490
- You know what we call you? 
- No.

936
01:07:54,530 --> 01:07:56,150
We call you the stupid Avenger.

937
01:07:56,530 --> 01:07:58,360
You're tiny Avenger!

938
01:08:01,160 --> 01:08:02,160
What, are you crazy?

939
01:08:02,370 --> 01:08:03,370
Yes.

940
01:08:03,540 --> 01:08:05,910
You know what? 
Earth does hate you.

941
01:08:26,730 --> 01:08:28,690
No.

942
01:08:31,190 --> 01:08:33,730
I'm sorry I said those things.

943
01:08:34,610 --> 01:08:35,860
You're not the stupid Avenger.

944
01:08:35,940 --> 01:08:37,990
Nobody calls you 
the stupid Avenger.

945
01:08:38,820 --> 01:08:40,120
It's okay.

946
01:08:40,490 --> 01:08:41,530
You just can't go around 
throwing shields

947
01:08:41,570 --> 01:08:42,740
at people. 
Could have killed me.

948
01:08:42,780 --> 01:08:43,990
I know. I'm sorry.

949
01:08:44,080 --> 01:08:45,750
I just get so angry 
all the time.

950
01:08:45,830 --> 01:08:47,870
Hulk always, always angry.

951
01:08:48,210 --> 01:08:50,420
I know. 
We're the same, you and I.

952
01:08:51,040 --> 01:08:52,590
We're just 
a couple of hot-headed fools.

953
01:08:52,840 --> 01:08:56,550
Yeah, same. Hulk like fire, 
Thor like water.

954
01:08:57,670 --> 01:08:59,260
We're kind of both like fire.

955
01:08:59,550 --> 01:09:01,430
But Hulk like real fire.

956
01:09:02,600 --> 01:09:04,850
Hulk like raging fire.

957
01:09:05,100 --> 01:09:07,230
Thor like smoldering fire.

958
01:09:09,850 --> 01:09:11,600
Hulk, I need you 
to do something for me.

959
01:09:18,280 --> 01:09:19,650
Angry girl.

960
01:09:27,120 --> 01:09:29,250
What's going on? 
What are you...

961
01:09:38,420 --> 01:09:40,170
You're so thick-headed 
that you can't tell...

962
01:09:40,430 --> 01:09:41,800
when someone's hiding 
all the way across

963
01:09:41,840 --> 01:09:43,390
the universe and wants 
to be left alone.

964
01:09:43,430 --> 01:09:45,930
- We need to talk. 
- No, you wanna talk to me.

965
01:09:46,810 --> 01:09:47,850
I need her to stay.

966
01:09:48,020 --> 01:09:49,020
Stay?

967
01:09:49,640 --> 01:09:50,640
Block.

968
01:09:52,400 --> 01:09:54,060
Stay.

969
01:09:54,150 --> 01:09:55,730
- Please. 
- Please.

970
01:09:58,530 --> 01:09:59,530
All right.

971
01:10:01,860 --> 01:10:03,570
Here's the deal.

972
01:10:04,280 --> 01:10:05,870
I'll listen to you...

973
01:10:06,700 --> 01:10:07,910
till this is empty.

974
01:10:09,540 --> 01:10:11,660
Asgard is in danger and 
people are dying.

975
01:10:11,960 --> 01:10:13,670
We need to get back there. 
I need your help.

976
01:10:15,590 --> 01:10:17,380
Finished. Bye.

977
01:10:19,130 --> 01:10:20,380
Odin is dead.

978
01:10:23,890 --> 01:10:25,970
Hela, the Goddess of Death, 
has invaded Asgard.

979
01:10:26,930 --> 01:10:29,390
If Hela's back, 
then Asgard's already lost.

980
01:10:29,720 --> 01:10:30,930
I'm going to stop her.

981
01:10:31,940 --> 01:10:32,940
- Alone? 
- Nope.

982
01:10:33,190 --> 01:10:34,400
I'm putting together a team.

983
01:10:34,730 --> 01:10:37,360
It's me, you, and the big guy.

984
01:10:37,860 --> 01:10:39,940
No. No team. Only Hulk.

985
01:10:40,240 --> 01:10:41,690
It's me and you.

986
01:10:42,070 --> 01:10:43,070
I think it's only you.

987
01:10:43,150 --> 01:10:45,450
Wait. Just listen. 
The Valkyrie are legend.

988
01:10:45,620 --> 01:10:47,950
Elite warriors of Asgard 
sworn to defend the throne.

989
01:10:48,950 --> 01:10:49,990
I'm not getting dragged into

990
01:10:50,040 --> 01:10:51,540
another one of Odin's 
family squabbles.

991
01:10:51,790 --> 01:10:53,580
- What's that supposed to mean? 
- Your sister.

992
01:10:53,710 --> 01:10:55,500
Her power comes from Asgard, 
same as yours.

993
01:10:55,790 --> 01:10:56,960
When it grew 
beyond Odin's control

994
01:10:57,000 --> 01:10:58,420
she massacred everyone 
in the palace...

995
01:10:58,460 --> 01:10:59,800
and tried to seize the throne.

996
01:11:00,250 --> 01:11:01,840
When she tried 
to escape her banishment...

997
01:11:01,880 --> 01:11:04,180
he sent the Valkyrie in 
to fight her back.

998
01:11:05,800 --> 01:11:07,800
I only survived because...

999
01:11:09,510 --> 01:11:10,930
Look, I already faced her once

1000
01:11:11,020 --> 01:11:12,770
back when I believed 
in the throne...

1001
01:11:13,060 --> 01:11:14,100
and it cost me everything.

1002
01:11:14,560 --> 01:11:15,940
That's what's wrong with Asgard.

1003
01:11:16,020 --> 01:11:18,400
The throne, the secrets, 
the whole golden sham.

1004
01:11:18,820 --> 01:11:19,940
I agree.

1005
01:11:20,980 --> 01:11:22,240
Don't get familiar.

1006
01:11:22,860 --> 01:11:24,110
I agree.

1007
01:11:24,400 --> 01:11:25,820
That's why I turned down 
the throne.

1008
01:11:26,070 --> 01:11:27,950
But this isn't about the crown.

1009
01:11:28,030 --> 01:11:29,080
This is about the people.

1010
01:11:29,370 --> 01:11:31,200
They're dying 
and they're your people, too.

1011
01:11:31,580 --> 01:11:32,830
Forget it.

1012
01:11:33,960 --> 01:11:35,210
I have.

1013
01:11:35,460 --> 01:11:36,540
- Okay. 
- Okay.

1014
01:11:36,790 --> 01:11:37,880
- Good. Great. 
- Great.

1015
01:11:38,080 --> 01:11:39,090
Thank you.

1016
01:11:39,210 --> 01:11:40,750
- For what? 
- For this.

1017
01:11:42,460 --> 01:11:44,300
Didn't see that, did you?

1018
01:11:45,970 --> 01:11:47,890
There... That's better.

1019
01:11:49,850 --> 01:11:51,470
You know, go ahead.

1020
01:11:51,760 --> 01:11:56,140
Stay here and enslave people 
for that lunatic.

1021
01:11:56,440 --> 01:11:57,690
Keep drinking, keep hiding.

1022
01:11:57,980 --> 01:11:59,060
But me...

1023
01:12:01,270 --> 01:12:02,980
I choose to run 
toward my problems

1024
01:12:03,070 --> 01:12:04,190
and not away from them.

1025
01:12:05,490 --> 01:12:06,570
Because that's what...

1026
01:12:11,780 --> 01:12:13,700
Because that's what heroes do.

1027
01:12:25,380 --> 01:12:26,670
Friend stay!

1028
01:12:38,690 --> 01:12:39,850
Yes!

1029
01:12:54,450 --> 01:12:55,450
All right.

1030
01:12:59,460 --> 01:13:00,460
Come on.

1031
01:13:03,130 --> 01:13:05,420
<i>Welcome. 
Voice activation required.</i>

1032
01:13:05,710 --> 01:13:07,220
Thor.

1033
01:13:07,300 --> 01:13:08,380
<i>Access denied.</i>

1034
01:13:09,010 --> 01:13:11,260
Thor, son of Odin.

1035
01:13:11,550 --> 01:13:12,550
<i>Access denied.</i>

1036
01:13:12,800 --> 01:13:13,810
God of Thunder.

1037
01:13:14,010 --> 01:13:15,140
<i>Access denied.</i>

1038
01:13:15,430 --> 01:13:16,430
Strongest Avenger.

1039
01:13:16,720 --> 01:13:17,930
<i>Access denied.</i>

1040
01:13:18,230 --> 01:13:19,600
Strongest Avenger.

1041
01:13:19,730 --> 01:13:21,060
<i>Access denied.</i>

1042
01:13:21,560 --> 01:13:23,560
Damn you, Stark.

1043
01:13:24,020 --> 01:13:25,020
Point Break.

1044
01:13:25,400 --> 01:13:27,400
<i>Welcome, Point Break.</i>

1045
01:13:29,200 --> 01:13:31,030
Friend stay!

1046
01:13:31,320 --> 01:13:33,320
No, no, no! Stop!

1047
01:13:33,410 --> 01:13:35,120
Stay!

1048
01:13:35,450 --> 01:13:36,700
Stop! 
Stop breaking everything!

1049
01:13:36,990 --> 01:13:38,330
Don't go!

1050
01:13:41,790 --> 01:13:42,960
<i>Nice work, big guy.</i>

1051
01:13:43,080 --> 01:13:44,500
<i>We don't know 
where Ultron's headed,</i>

1052
01:13:44,540 --> 01:13:46,590
<i>but you're going very high, 
very fast.</i>

1053
01:13:46,880 --> 01:13:48,670
<i>So, I need you to turn 
this bird around, okay?</i>

1054
01:13:49,170 --> 01:13:51,590
<i>We can't track you 
in stealth mode...</i>

1055
01:13:52,010 --> 01:13:53,510
<i>so I need you 
to help me out. Okay?</i>

1056
01:13:57,390 --> 01:13:58,770
<i>I need you to...</i>

1057
01:14:14,870 --> 01:14:17,240
No! No, Banner!

1058
01:14:24,830 --> 01:14:26,000
Jeez.

1059
01:14:27,090 --> 01:14:28,420
Banner.

1060
01:14:29,670 --> 01:14:31,130
Hey, hey, hey.

1061
01:14:31,380 --> 01:14:32,720
You all right, Banner?

1062
01:14:35,300 --> 01:14:37,050
Sun's going down. 
Sun's going down.

1063
01:14:37,720 --> 01:14:38,890
That's it, breathe.

1064
01:14:39,600 --> 01:14:41,430
I won't hurt you.

1065
01:14:42,350 --> 01:14:43,350
Sun's going down.

1066
01:14:43,600 --> 01:14:44,900
- Thor. 
- Yeah.

1067
01:14:45,900 --> 01:14:47,150
What happened to your hair?

1068
01:14:47,400 --> 01:14:48,650
Some creepy old man cut it off.

1069
01:14:48,900 --> 01:14:50,190
- It looks good. 
- Thanks.

1070
01:14:50,490 --> 01:14:52,610
Where are we? How's Nat?

1071
01:14:53,200 --> 01:14:55,820
- Nat is good, I'm sure. 
- Is she okay?

1072
01:14:56,160 --> 01:14:57,830
- And what about Sokovia? 
- Sokovia?

1073
01:14:58,120 --> 01:14:59,450
The city, Sokovia. 
Did we save it?

1074
01:14:59,790 --> 01:15:00,830
- Banner, listen. 
- What?

1075
01:15:01,080 --> 01:15:02,960
Sokovia. Ultron. 
That was two years ago.

1076
01:15:03,290 --> 01:15:04,670
- What are you saying? 
- Well...

1077
01:15:04,920 --> 01:15:05,920
What?

1078
01:15:06,830 --> 01:15:08,090
I've been Hulk for two years?

1079
01:15:08,590 --> 01:15:09,840
I'm afraid so.

1080
01:15:16,050 --> 01:15:17,050
What the hell happened?

1081
01:15:20,770 --> 01:15:22,390
Banner, there's something 
you should know.

1082
01:15:24,850 --> 01:15:25,900
<i>Voice activation required.</i>

1083
01:15:25,980 --> 01:15:26,980
Banner.

1084
01:15:27,190 --> 01:15:28,610
<i>Welcome, strongest Avenger.</i>

1085
01:15:28,810 --> 01:15:29,820
What?

1086
01:15:29,900 --> 01:15:30,900
Ship's log.

1087
01:15:42,450 --> 01:15:43,910
Thor, where are we?

1088
01:15:44,210 --> 01:15:45,210
Yeah, about that.

1089
01:15:45,370 --> 01:15:46,620
<i>Sakaar, hear ye.</i>

1090
01:15:46,710 --> 01:15:48,420
<i>Attention please. 
I have some bad news.</i>

1091
01:15:48,670 --> 01:15:51,340
<i>My beloved exalted champion 
has turned up missing.</i>

1092
01:15:51,550 --> 01:15:53,800
<i>Take to the streets. 
Celebrate my champion.</i>

1093
01:15:53,880 --> 01:15:54,880
Who's that?

1094
01:15:55,220 --> 01:15:56,720
He kind of runs the place.

1095
01:15:57,640 --> 01:15:58,930
You actually lived 
at his house for awhile.

1096
01:15:58,970 --> 01:15:59,970
- I did? 
- Yeah.

1097
01:16:00,350 --> 01:16:02,520
Quite a lot's happened. You 
and I had a fight recently.

1098
01:16:02,890 --> 01:16:04,600
- Did I win? 
- No, I won. Easily.

1099
01:16:05,060 --> 01:16:06,060
Doesn't sound right.

1100
01:16:06,140 --> 01:16:07,140
Well, it's true.

1101
01:16:07,230 --> 01:16:09,270
<i>It seems that that 
criminally seductive</i>

1102
01:16:09,360 --> 01:16:11,690
<i>Lord of Thunder 
has stolen him away.</i>

1103
01:16:12,070 --> 01:16:14,360
Seductive God of Thunder. 
We need to move.

1104
01:16:15,320 --> 01:16:16,320
No.

1105
01:16:18,200 --> 01:16:19,280
This is bad.

1106
01:16:19,490 --> 01:16:21,330
This is really, really bad.

1107
01:16:24,290 --> 01:16:27,750
Thor, I think I'm freaking out.

1108
01:16:28,290 --> 01:16:29,330
No, no, no.

1109
01:16:29,500 --> 01:16:31,340
Don't freak out. You're okay. 
Put these on.

1110
01:16:31,590 --> 01:16:32,630
These are Tony's clothes.

1111
01:16:32,800 --> 01:16:34,050
- I know, come on. 
- Is he here?

1112
01:16:34,300 --> 01:16:36,260
No, he's not here. But listen. 
Just stay calm, okay?

1113
01:16:36,300 --> 01:16:38,380
The sun's going down. 
The sun's getting really low.

1114
01:16:38,470 --> 01:16:39,470
Sun's going down.

1115
01:16:47,270 --> 01:16:49,060
I'm upset!

1116
01:16:52,150 --> 01:16:53,940
I'm very upset.

1117
01:16:54,230 --> 01:16:56,190
You know what I like about 
being upset? The blame.

1118
01:16:56,440 --> 01:16:58,530
Right now, that's 
the mindset that I'm in.

1119
01:16:58,610 --> 01:16:59,780
And you know who I'm blaming?

1120
01:16:59,990 --> 01:17:01,370
- Grandmaster, I can... 
- Hey!

1121
01:17:01,530 --> 01:17:02,530
Don't interrupt me!

1122
01:17:02,740 --> 01:17:03,740
Here you go.

1123
01:17:04,660 --> 01:17:06,120
Why are you handing me 
the melt stick?

1124
01:17:06,200 --> 01:17:07,830
He was interrupting.

1125
01:17:08,210 --> 01:17:09,870
That's not a capital violation.

1126
01:17:10,170 --> 01:17:11,330
Where was I?

1127
01:17:11,880 --> 01:17:14,210
My precious champion 
has come up missing...

1128
01:17:14,500 --> 01:17:16,460
and it's all because 
of that Lord of Thunder.

1129
01:17:16,550 --> 01:17:18,720
It's all because of him. 
Your brother.

1130
01:17:19,010 --> 01:17:21,840
Whatever the story is. 
Adopted, or complicated.

1131
01:17:22,010 --> 01:17:23,220
I'm sure there's a big history.

1132
01:17:23,260 --> 01:17:24,260
And your contender...

1133
01:17:25,010 --> 01:17:26,020
My dear friend...

1134
01:17:26,430 --> 01:17:28,140
if you were to give me 12 hours,

1135
01:17:28,230 --> 01:17:29,810
I could bring them both 
back to you. Alive.

1136
01:17:29,850 --> 01:17:31,270
I could do it in two.

1137
01:17:32,270 --> 01:17:33,270
I could do it in one.

1138
01:17:33,520 --> 01:17:34,520
Let's stop there.

1139
01:17:34,730 --> 01:17:36,440
You know what? 
I woke up this morning

1140
01:17:36,530 --> 01:17:38,240
thinking about 
a public execution.

1141
01:17:39,280 --> 01:17:40,570
But for now, I'll settle 
for this sweet little...

1142
01:17:40,610 --> 01:17:43,320
"Who's gonna get him first?"

1143
01:17:44,410 --> 01:17:46,910
So, you're on the clock.

1144
01:17:48,910 --> 01:17:49,100
What have you done?

1145
01:17:50,080 --> 01:17:51,330
I don't answer to you, lackey.

1146
01:17:51,460 --> 01:17:52,460
It's Loki.

1147
01:17:52,670 --> 01:17:54,170
And you will answer 
to the Grandmaster.

1148
01:17:57,420 --> 01:18:00,130
Why would you help my brother 
escape with that green fool?

1149
01:18:00,550 --> 01:18:01,680
I don't help anyone.

1150
01:18:08,350 --> 01:18:09,350
You're a Valkyrie.

1151
01:18:14,440 --> 01:18:16,480
I thought the Valkyrie had 
all died gruesome deaths.

1152
01:18:17,860 --> 01:18:19,360
Choose your next words wisely.

1153
01:18:19,690 --> 01:18:22,780
I'm terribly sorry. 
Must be a very painful memory.

1154
01:19:15,750 --> 01:19:18,090
The sun's going down. 
It's getting really low.

1155
01:19:19,420 --> 01:19:20,630
The sun's going down.

1156
01:19:20,710 --> 01:19:22,130
- It's getting real low. 
- Shoot.

1157
01:19:22,510 --> 01:19:24,720
- Sun's getting low. 
- Would you stop saying that?

1158
01:19:24,800 --> 01:19:25,970
I just need you to stay calm.

1159
01:19:26,090 --> 01:19:27,930
Calm? I'm on an alien planet!

1160
01:19:28,220 --> 01:19:29,890
It's just a planet. You've 
been on a planet before.

1161
01:19:29,930 --> 01:19:30,970
Yeah. One.

1162
01:19:31,310 --> 01:19:33,020
Now you've been on two. 
That's a good thing.

1163
01:19:33,140 --> 01:19:34,270
It's a new experience.

1164
01:19:34,480 --> 01:19:36,400
My neurons, 
they're firing faster

1165
01:19:36,480 --> 01:19:38,480
than my brain can handle 
the information.

1166
01:19:38,730 --> 01:19:40,900
The whole thing is totally 
different this time.

1167
01:19:41,190 --> 01:19:42,900
In the past, I always felt 
like Hulk and I

1168
01:19:42,990 --> 01:19:44,280
each had a hand on the wheel.

1169
01:19:44,650 --> 01:19:46,320
But this time, it's like 
he had the keys

1170
01:19:46,410 --> 01:19:47,990
to the car and I was 
locked in the trunk.

1171
01:19:48,200 --> 01:19:50,160
All right, well, you're back 
now. That's all that matters.

1172
01:19:50,200 --> 01:19:51,240
No, it's not what matters.

1173
01:19:51,450 --> 01:19:52,540
What I'm trying 
to tell you, is that

1174
01:19:52,580 --> 01:19:54,120
if I turn into the Hulk again...

1175
01:19:54,370 --> 01:19:55,750
Banner may never come back.

1176
01:19:56,040 --> 01:19:57,250
And we're stranded on a planet

1177
01:19:57,330 --> 01:19:59,080
that is designed 
to stress me out.

1178
01:19:59,170 --> 01:20:00,290
We're not stranded.

1179
01:20:00,380 --> 01:20:02,000
I'm gonna figure out a way 
to get us home.

1180
01:20:02,250 --> 01:20:03,260
Thank you.

1181
01:20:03,590 --> 01:20:05,590
Not your home, though. Asgard. 
My home.

1182
01:20:05,930 --> 01:20:06,970
What?

1183
01:20:07,220 --> 01:20:08,800
Listen, my people 
are in great danger.

1184
01:20:09,390 --> 01:20:11,640
You and I, we have to fight 
this really powerful being...

1185
01:20:11,810 --> 01:20:13,560
who also happens 
to be my sister.

1186
01:20:13,810 --> 01:20:15,480
Okay, that is so wrong 
on so many...

1187
01:20:15,680 --> 01:20:16,810
I don't wanna fight your sister.

1188
01:20:16,850 --> 01:20:18,100
That's a family issue.

1189
01:20:18,230 --> 01:20:19,480
No, she's an evil being.

1190
01:20:19,560 --> 01:20:21,360
I don't care what she is.

1191
01:20:21,440 --> 01:20:23,610
I'm not fighting any 
more beings. I'm sick of it.

1192
01:20:23,860 --> 01:20:24,860
- What? 
- I just told you.

1193
01:20:25,190 --> 01:20:26,700
If I turn into the Hulk,

1194
01:20:26,780 --> 01:20:28,070
I am never gonna 
come back again.

1195
01:20:28,160 --> 01:20:29,200
And you don't care.

1196
01:20:29,370 --> 01:20:31,080
No, no. I'm putting together 
the team.

1197
01:20:31,370 --> 01:20:32,580
The Hulk is the fire.

1198
01:20:32,870 --> 01:20:34,660
Wait, you're just using me 
to get to the Hulk.

1199
01:20:34,790 --> 01:20:36,210
- What? No! 
- It's gross.

1200
01:20:36,460 --> 01:20:38,250
You don't care about me. 
You're not my friend.

1201
01:20:38,500 --> 01:20:40,130
No! I don't even 
like the Hulk.

1202
01:20:40,210 --> 01:20:41,460
He's all like...

1203
01:20:41,630 --> 01:20:43,050
"Smash, smash, smash."

1204
01:20:43,300 --> 01:20:44,300
I prefer you.

1205
01:20:45,210 --> 01:20:46,220
Thanks.

1206
01:20:47,090 --> 01:20:48,590
But if I'm being honest,

1207
01:20:48,680 --> 01:20:50,220
when it comes 
to fighting evil beings...

1208
01:20:50,300 --> 01:20:51,600
he is very powerful and useful.

1209
01:20:51,930 --> 01:20:53,720
Yeah, Banner's powerful 
and useful, too.

1210
01:20:54,010 --> 01:20:55,100
Is he though?

1211
01:20:55,390 --> 01:20:57,390
How many PhDs 
does Hulk have? Zero.

1212
01:20:57,600 --> 01:20:59,350
How many PhDs does 
Banner have? Seven.

1213
01:21:00,310 --> 01:21:02,190
Fine, you don't have 
to fight anyone.

1214
01:21:02,440 --> 01:21:04,230
But we're in danger here, 
so we have to move.

1215
01:21:08,360 --> 01:21:09,530
What are you doing with that?

1216
01:21:09,570 --> 01:21:10,610
I need a disguise. 
I'm a fugitive.

1217
01:21:10,660 --> 01:21:12,370
- I need a disguise. 
- You are the disguise.

1218
01:21:13,200 --> 01:21:14,660
- I'll be Tony Stark. 
- What?

1219
01:21:15,040 --> 01:21:16,620
Yeah. Tony and the gypsy.

1220
01:21:16,950 --> 01:21:19,330
No, no, you're not Tony. 
You're Bruce. Bruce Banner.

1221
01:21:19,580 --> 01:21:21,000
Then why did you dress me up 
like Tony?

1222
01:21:21,040 --> 01:21:22,040
Because you were naked.

1223
01:21:22,210 --> 01:21:23,340
Okay, I'll give you that.

1224
01:21:24,250 --> 01:21:25,500
What are you doing? 
Stop doing that!

1225
01:21:25,550 --> 01:21:26,920
Tony wears his pants 
super tight.

1226
01:21:27,010 --> 01:21:28,010
- Stop it! 
- I'm sorry.

1227
01:21:28,340 --> 01:21:30,340
- Why are you being so weird? 
- I don't know.

1228
01:21:30,630 --> 01:21:32,890
Maybe the fact that I was 
trapped for two years...

1229
01:21:33,100 --> 01:21:35,510
inside of a monster 
made me a little weird.

1230
01:21:35,890 --> 01:21:37,430
Hey. It's okay.

1231
01:21:37,680 --> 01:21:39,980
You're good. Calm down. 
Come on.

1232
01:21:40,230 --> 01:21:41,600
Listen, we're gonna 
go to Asgard...

1233
01:21:41,770 --> 01:21:42,810
and you're not gonna 
have to think about

1234
01:21:42,860 --> 01:21:43,860
the Hulk ever again.

1235
01:21:44,150 --> 01:21:45,190
- All right? 
- All right.

1236
01:21:49,280 --> 01:21:50,950
Hulk!

1237
01:21:52,910 --> 01:21:54,490
This is bad.

1238
01:21:58,660 --> 01:21:59,100
Banner! Banner!

1239
01:22:04,040 --> 01:22:05,090
Banner!

1240
01:22:18,770 --> 01:22:19,810
Banner!

1241
01:22:20,350 --> 01:22:21,480
Thor!

1242
01:22:32,780 --> 01:22:33,780
Hi.

1243
01:22:34,070 --> 01:22:35,070
Hi.

1244
01:22:35,320 --> 01:22:36,580
I was gonna do that.

1245
01:22:36,660 --> 01:22:37,790
Yeah, well, I did it first.

1246
01:22:38,160 --> 01:22:39,950
That's good. 
What are you doing here?

1247
01:22:40,100 --> 01:22:42,750
What are you doing here? 
I thought you were leaving.

1248
01:22:42,790 --> 01:22:43,790
I got sidetracked.

1249
01:22:44,250 --> 01:22:45,250
What's with the...

1250
01:22:45,750 --> 01:22:46,840
It's my disguise.

1251
01:22:47,000 --> 01:22:48,000
But I can see your face.

1252
01:22:48,500 --> 01:22:50,090
Not when I do this, you can't.

1253
01:22:50,880 --> 01:22:52,680
Your hair looks nice. 
I like what you did with it.

1254
01:22:52,720 --> 01:22:54,130
Change it? Washed it maybe?

1255
01:23:00,350 --> 01:23:01,640
What are those things 
on her eyes?

1256
01:23:01,680 --> 01:23:03,190
Are those the people 
that she's killed?

1257
01:23:03,270 --> 01:23:04,980
She's so beautiful and strong 
and courageous.

1258
01:23:05,020 --> 01:23:06,020
Who is this guy?

1259
01:23:06,110 --> 01:23:07,150
- He's a friend. 
- Who? Me?

1260
01:23:07,190 --> 01:23:08,650
- I'm Bruce. 
- I feel like I know you.

1261
01:23:08,770 --> 01:23:10,690
I feel like I know you, too.

1262
01:23:15,360 --> 01:23:17,240
Look, I've spent years 
in a haze,

1263
01:23:17,320 --> 01:23:18,700
trying to forget my past.

1264
01:23:19,240 --> 01:23:20,540
Sakaar seemed like 
the best place

1265
01:23:20,620 --> 01:23:22,870
to drink and forget, 
and to die one day.

1266
01:23:23,250 --> 01:23:24,870
I was thinking 
that you drink too much,

1267
01:23:24,960 --> 01:23:26,380
and that probably 
was gonna kill you.

1268
01:23:26,500 --> 01:23:27,710
I don't plan to stop drinking.

1269
01:23:27,750 --> 01:23:29,960
But I don't wanna forget.

1270
01:23:30,210 --> 01:23:31,760
I can't turn away anymore...

1271
01:23:32,510 --> 01:23:34,170
so if I'm gonna die...

1272
01:23:34,470 --> 01:23:36,050
well, it may as well be 
driving my sword

1273
01:23:36,140 --> 01:23:37,680
through the heart 
of that murderous hag.

1274
01:23:37,800 --> 01:23:39,260
- Good. 
- Yeah.

1275
01:23:39,560 --> 01:23:42,430
So, I'm saying 
that I wanna be on the team.

1276
01:23:43,140 --> 01:23:44,350
Has it got a name?

1277
01:23:44,560 --> 01:23:47,230
Yeah, it's called the Revengers.

1278
01:23:47,600 --> 01:23:48,610
Revengers?

1279
01:23:48,690 --> 01:23:51,070
Because I'm getting revenge. 
You're getting revenge.

1280
01:23:52,940 --> 01:23:54,240
Do you want revenge?

1281
01:23:54,400 --> 01:23:56,530
I'm undecided.

1282
01:23:56,820 --> 01:23:57,820
Okay.

1283
01:23:58,490 --> 01:24:00,200
Also, I've got a peace offering.

1284
01:24:03,500 --> 01:24:05,330
Surprise.

1285
01:24:12,460 --> 01:24:13,800
Just had to be sure.

1286
01:24:17,590 --> 01:24:18,590
Hello, Bruce.

1287
01:24:20,010 --> 01:24:21,760
So, last time I saw you,

1288
01:24:21,850 --> 01:24:23,180
you were trying 
to kill everybody.

1289
01:24:23,270 --> 01:24:24,390
Where are you at these days?

1290
01:24:24,930 --> 01:24:26,640
It varies from moment to moment.

1291
01:24:27,480 --> 01:24:28,940
Is that a Dragonfang?

1292
01:24:29,610 --> 01:24:30,690
It is.

1293
01:24:30,770 --> 01:24:31,820
My God.

1294
01:24:32,900 --> 01:24:34,860
This is the famed sword 
of the Valkyrie.

1295
01:24:34,940 --> 01:24:36,780
Sakaar and Asgard 
are about as far apart

1296
01:24:36,860 --> 01:24:38,030
as any two known systems.

1297
01:24:38,530 --> 01:24:41,030
Our best bet is a wormhole 
just outside of city limits.

1298
01:24:41,450 --> 01:24:43,330
Refuel on Xandar, and 
we can be back in Asgard

1299
01:24:43,410 --> 01:24:44,870
in 18 months.

1300
01:24:45,160 --> 01:24:48,290
Nope. We are going through 
the big one.

1301
01:24:48,540 --> 01:24:49,540
The Devil's Anus?

1302
01:24:49,920 --> 01:24:50,920
Anus?

1303
01:24:51,080 --> 01:24:52,250
Wait, wait, wait. Whose anus?

1304
01:24:52,290 --> 01:24:53,340
For the record, I didn't know

1305
01:24:53,380 --> 01:24:54,420
it was called that 
when I picked it.

1306
01:24:54,460 --> 01:24:56,090
That looks like 
a collapsing neutron star...

1307
01:24:56,130 --> 01:24:58,550
inside of an 
Einstein-Rosen Bridge.

1308
01:24:58,970 --> 01:25:00,140
We need another ship.

1309
01:25:00,220 --> 01:25:01,640
That would tear mine to pieces.

1310
01:25:01,930 --> 01:25:03,510
She's right. We need one 
that can withstand

1311
01:25:03,560 --> 01:25:04,890
the geodetic strain 
from the singularity.

1312
01:25:04,930 --> 01:25:06,770
And has an offline 
power steering system...

1313
01:25:06,850 --> 01:25:09,480
that could also function 
without the on-board computer.

1314
01:25:09,770 --> 01:25:11,060
And we need one 
with cup holders,

1315
01:25:11,150 --> 01:25:12,690
because we're gonna die. 
So, drinks!

1316
01:25:13,070 --> 01:25:14,860
Do I know you? 
I feel like I know you.

1317
01:25:15,110 --> 01:25:16,860
I feel like I know you, too. 
It's weird.

1318
01:25:17,110 --> 01:25:18,110
What do you say?

1319
01:25:18,450 --> 01:25:19,490
Uncharted metagalactic travel

1320
01:25:19,530 --> 01:25:20,860
through a volatile 
cosmic gateway.

1321
01:25:21,070 --> 01:25:22,160
Talk about an adventure.

1322
01:25:22,910 --> 01:25:24,450
- We need a ship. 
- Need a ship.

1323
01:25:24,700 --> 01:25:25,740
There are one or two ships.

1324
01:25:25,790 --> 01:25:26,910
Absolute top of the line 
models...

1325
01:25:26,950 --> 01:25:28,250
I don't mean to impose...

1326
01:25:31,710 --> 01:25:33,380
But the Grandmaster 
has a great many ships.

1327
01:25:33,960 --> 01:25:35,340
I may even have stolen

1328
01:25:35,420 --> 01:25:37,380
the access codes 
to his security system.

1329
01:25:37,670 --> 01:25:38,720
And suddenly you're overcome

1330
01:25:38,760 --> 01:25:40,090
with an urge 
to do the right thing.

1331
01:25:40,130 --> 01:25:41,130
Heavens, no.

1332
01:25:41,220 --> 01:25:42,890
I've run out of favor 
with the Grandmaster...

1333
01:25:42,930 --> 01:25:44,850
and in exchange for codes 
and access to a ship...

1334
01:25:45,060 --> 01:25:48,100
I'm asking for safe passage 
through the Anus.

1335
01:25:48,480 --> 01:25:49,850
You're telling us 
that you can get us

1336
01:25:49,890 --> 01:25:51,020
access into the garage...

1337
01:25:51,100 --> 01:25:52,730
without setting off any alarms?

1338
01:25:53,190 --> 01:25:54,730
Yes, brother. I can.

1339
01:25:54,980 --> 01:25:57,650
Okay, can I just... 
A quick FYI.

1340
01:25:57,940 --> 01:25:59,740
I was just talking to him 
just a couple minutes ago...

1341
01:25:59,780 --> 01:26:02,160
and he was totally ready 
to kill any of us.

1342
01:26:02,410 --> 01:26:03,490
He did try to kill me.

1343
01:26:03,780 --> 01:26:05,490
Yes, me too. 
On many, many occasions.

1344
01:26:05,780 --> 01:26:07,450
There was one time 
when we were children...

1345
01:26:07,490 --> 01:26:08,950
he transformed himself 
into a snake,

1346
01:26:09,040 --> 01:26:10,330
and he knows that I love snakes.

1347
01:26:10,410 --> 01:26:12,250
So, I went to pick up 
the snake to admire it...

1348
01:26:12,420 --> 01:26:13,830
and he transformed back 
into himself

1349
01:26:13,920 --> 01:26:15,210
and he was like, 
"Yeah, it's me!"

1350
01:26:15,290 --> 01:26:18,170
And he stabbed me. 
We were eight at the time.

1351
01:26:18,800 --> 01:26:19,880
If we're boosting a ship...

1352
01:26:20,050 --> 01:26:21,760
we're gonna need to draw some 
guards away from the palace.

1353
01:26:21,800 --> 01:26:23,090
Why not set the beast loose?

1354
01:26:23,300 --> 01:26:24,300
Shut up.

1355
01:26:24,550 --> 01:26:25,550
You guys have a beast?

1356
01:26:25,760 --> 01:26:28,060
No, there's no beast. 
He's just being stupid.

1357
01:26:28,390 --> 01:26:29,770
We're going to start 
a revolution.

1358
01:26:29,850 --> 01:26:31,310
- Revolution? 
- I'll explain later.

1359
01:26:31,890 --> 01:26:34,060
- Who's this guy again? 
- I'll explain later.

1360
01:26:35,270 --> 01:26:37,400
Is that some sort of protoplasm,

1361
01:26:37,480 --> 01:26:38,730
all the stuff 
that's coming out of you...

1362
01:26:38,780 --> 01:26:39,940
or are they eggs?

1363
01:26:41,450 --> 01:26:42,570
Looks like eggs.

1364
01:26:52,120 --> 01:26:53,330
I'm looking for Korg.

1365
01:26:53,710 --> 01:26:54,880
Who's asking?

1366
01:26:55,130 --> 01:26:56,210
I know you're asking.

1367
01:26:56,500 --> 01:26:58,380
Is anyone else asking, 
or is it just you?

1368
01:26:58,710 --> 01:27:00,670
The Lord of Thunder 
sends his best.

1369
01:27:04,340 --> 01:27:06,350
The revolution has begun.

1370
01:27:06,680 --> 01:27:08,600
Revolution? 
How did this happen?

1371
01:27:08,890 --> 01:27:10,310
Don't know.

1372
01:27:10,600 --> 01:27:11,980
But the arena's mainframe

1373
01:27:12,060 --> 01:27:13,850
for the Obedience Disks 
have been deactivated...

1374
01:27:13,890 --> 01:27:15,810
and the slaves 
have armed themselves.

1375
01:27:15,980 --> 01:27:17,940
I don't like that word.

1376
01:27:18,190 --> 01:27:19,400
Which? Mainframe?

1377
01:27:19,650 --> 01:27:21,650
No. Why would I not like 
"mainframe"?

1378
01:27:21,900 --> 01:27:23,860
No, the "S" word.

1379
01:27:24,110 --> 01:27:26,660
Sorry, the prisoners with jobs 
have armed themselves.

1380
01:27:28,200 --> 01:27:29,410
Okay, that's better.

1381
01:27:35,710 --> 01:27:37,420
Hey, so, listen. 
We should talk.

1382
01:27:38,880 --> 01:27:39,920
I disagree.

1383
01:27:40,420 --> 01:27:43,220
Open communication 
was never our family's forte.

1384
01:27:43,590 --> 01:27:44,590
You have no idea.

1385
01:27:44,760 --> 01:27:47,340
Been quite the revelation 
since we last spoke.

1386
01:27:47,430 --> 01:27:48,430
Hello.

1387
01:27:49,510 --> 01:27:50,510
Hi.

1388
01:27:57,600 --> 01:27:59,150
Odin brought us together.

1389
01:28:00,230 --> 01:28:03,030
It's almost poetic that his 
death should split us apart.

1390
01:28:09,160 --> 01:28:11,160
We might as well be 
strangers now.

1391
01:28:11,410 --> 01:28:14,370
Two sons of the crown, 
set adrift.

1392
01:28:17,620 --> 01:28:19,130
Thought you didn't 
wanna talk about it.

1393
01:28:20,540 --> 01:28:21,550
Here's the thing.

1394
01:28:21,920 --> 01:28:23,760
I'm probably better off 
staying here on Sakaar.

1395
01:28:23,800 --> 01:28:25,420
That's exactly 
what I was thinking.

1396
01:28:27,470 --> 01:28:28,760
Did you just agree with me?

1397
01:28:29,050 --> 01:28:30,550
Come on, this place 
is perfect for you.

1398
01:28:30,800 --> 01:28:32,390
It's savage, chaotic, lawless...

1399
01:28:32,600 --> 01:28:34,180
Brother, you're gonna do 
great here.

1400
01:28:34,430 --> 01:28:36,020
Do you truly think 
so little of me?

1401
01:28:38,270 --> 01:28:39,900
Loki, I thought 
the world of you.

1402
01:28:41,110 --> 01:28:43,570
I thought we were gonna fight 
side by side forever.

1403
01:28:43,860 --> 01:28:46,570
But at the end of the day, 
you're you and I'm me.

1404
01:28:47,360 --> 01:28:49,740
I don't know, maybe 
there's still good in you.

1405
01:28:49,990 --> 01:28:51,160
But let's be honest,

1406
01:28:51,240 --> 01:28:53,410
our paths diverged 
a long time ago.

1407
01:28:58,210 --> 01:28:59,210
Yeah.

1408
01:29:00,420 --> 01:29:01,460
It's probably for the best

1409
01:29:01,540 --> 01:29:02,920
that we never 
see each other again.

1410
01:29:02,960 --> 01:29:04,170
That's what you always wanted.

1411
01:29:08,470 --> 01:29:10,050
Hey, let's do "Get Help."

1412
01:29:10,300 --> 01:29:11,300
- What? 
- "Get Help."

1413
01:29:11,390 --> 01:29:12,390
No.

1414
01:29:12,470 --> 01:29:13,510
- Come on, you love it. 
- I hate it.

1415
01:29:13,560 --> 01:29:14,600
It's great. 
It works every time.

1416
01:29:14,640 --> 01:29:16,310
- It's humiliating. 
- Do you have a better plan?

1417
01:29:16,350 --> 01:29:17,890
- No. 
- We're doing it.

1418
01:29:18,060 --> 01:29:19,730
We are not doing "Get Help."

1419
01:29:20,350 --> 01:29:22,020
Get help! Please!

1420
01:29:22,270 --> 01:29:23,270
My brother, he's dying.

1421
01:29:23,480 --> 01:29:25,400
Get help! Help him!

1422
01:29:27,570 --> 01:29:28,700
Classic.

1423
01:29:28,860 --> 01:29:30,200
Still hate it.

1424
01:29:30,410 --> 01:29:32,660
- It's humiliating. 
- Not for me, it's not.

1425
01:29:32,910 --> 01:29:34,950
Now, which one's the ship 
she told us to get?

1426
01:29:35,040 --> 01:29:36,040
<i>The Commodore.</i>

1427
01:29:36,950 --> 01:29:37,950
Right.

1428
01:29:40,710 --> 01:29:43,210
Though I feel it won't make 
much of a difference.

1429
01:29:45,460 --> 01:29:47,130
Loki.

1430
01:29:48,380 --> 01:29:49,840
I know I've betrayed you 
many times before...

1431
01:29:49,880 --> 01:29:51,510
but this time 
it's truly nothing personal.

1432
01:29:51,760 --> 01:29:53,550
The reward for your capture

1433
01:29:53,640 --> 01:29:54,720
will set me up nicely.

1434
01:29:55,010 --> 01:29:56,430
Never one for sentiment, 
were you?

1435
01:29:56,810 --> 01:29:58,060
Easier to let it burn.

1436
01:29:58,390 --> 01:29:59,390
I agree.

1437
01:30:08,070 --> 01:30:09,570
That looks painful.

1438
01:30:10,360 --> 01:30:13,030
Dear brother, 
you're becoming predictable.

1439
01:30:13,410 --> 01:30:15,200
I trust you, you betray me.

1440
01:30:15,530 --> 01:30:17,450
Round and round 
in circles we go.

1441
01:30:17,740 --> 01:30:19,620
See, Loki, life is about, 
it's about growth.

1442
01:30:19,910 --> 01:30:21,040
It's about change.

1443
01:30:21,290 --> 01:30:24,250
But you seem to 
just wanna stay the same.

1444
01:30:25,040 --> 01:30:26,590
I guess 
what I'm trying to say...

1445
01:30:26,840 --> 01:30:29,670
is that you'll always be 
the God of Mischief...

1446
01:30:29,970 --> 01:30:31,300
but you could be more.

1447
01:30:33,930 --> 01:30:35,850
I'll just put this over here 
for you.

1448
01:30:36,470 --> 01:30:39,810
Anyway, all got places to be, 
so good luck.

1449
01:30:45,270 --> 01:30:46,570
All right, 
I can figure this out.

1450
01:30:46,980 --> 01:30:48,730
It's just another spaceship.

1451
01:31:02,160 --> 01:31:03,460
<i>Loyal Sakaarians...</i>

1452
01:31:03,710 --> 01:31:05,580
<i>Lord of Thunder 
has stolen my ship</i>

1453
01:31:05,670 --> 01:31:07,040
<i>and my favorite champion.</i>

1454
01:31:08,670 --> 01:31:11,760
<i>Sakaarians, take to the skies. 
Bring him down.</i>

1455
01:31:11,970 --> 01:31:13,590
<i>Do not let him 
leave this planet.</i>

1456
01:31:26,810 --> 01:31:28,060
- Good shot! 
- Thanks.

1457
01:31:31,150 --> 01:31:32,150
<i>Open the doors.</i>

1458
01:31:32,240 --> 01:31:33,530
Okay.

1459
01:31:38,910 --> 01:31:40,660
I hope that you're tougher 
than you look.

1460
01:31:40,830 --> 01:31:41,870
Why?

1461
01:31:54,420 --> 01:31:56,130
Shouldn't we be shooting back 
or something?

1462
01:31:56,220 --> 01:31:57,220
Yes, we should.

1463
01:32:17,700 --> 01:32:18,990
No!

1464
01:32:21,990 --> 01:32:22,990
- No! 
- No!

1465
01:32:30,000 --> 01:32:31,040
Get inside!

1466
01:32:31,340 --> 01:32:32,750
In a minute.

1467
01:32:44,180 --> 01:32:46,060
I should probably go and help. 
Here, take the wheel.

1468
01:32:46,100 --> 01:32:47,690
No. I don't know 
how to fly one of these.

1469
01:32:47,770 --> 01:32:49,520
You're a scientist. 
Use one of your PhDs.

1470
01:32:49,600 --> 01:32:52,820
None of them are for flying 
alien spaceships!

1471
01:33:27,600 --> 01:33:28,600
Okay, come on.

1472
01:33:28,690 --> 01:33:30,730
There's gotta be a gun 
on this thing.

1473
01:33:30,850 --> 01:33:31,860
That looks like a gun.

1474
01:33:33,190 --> 01:33:34,480
<i>It's my birthday</i>

1475
01:33:34,570 --> 01:33:35,610
<i>It's my birthday</i>

1476
01:33:36,570 --> 01:33:37,570
<i>It's my birthday</i>

1477
01:33:45,620 --> 01:33:46,700
Yeah!

1478
01:34:04,260 --> 01:34:06,350
Guys, we're coming up 
on the Devil's Anus!

1479
01:34:13,150 --> 01:34:14,150
There she is.

1480
01:34:14,440 --> 01:34:16,270
Our ticket out of here.

1481
01:34:16,940 --> 01:34:18,110
Hey, what's this?

1482
01:34:23,160 --> 01:34:24,240
Thank you.

1483
01:34:24,320 --> 01:34:26,830
Hey, man. We're about to jump 
on that ginormous spaceship.

1484
01:34:26,910 --> 01:34:27,910
You wanna come?

1485
01:34:28,290 --> 01:34:30,910
You do seem like

1486
01:34:30,100 --> 01:34:32,500
you're in desperate need 
of leadership.

1487
01:34:32,920 --> 01:34:34,330
Why, thank you.

1488
01:34:38,210 --> 01:34:39,210
Here we go.

1489
01:34:45,760 --> 01:34:46,760
Shit.

1490
01:35:04,320 --> 01:35:06,030
Asgardians...

1491
01:35:06,280 --> 01:35:08,700
some misguided soul...

1492
01:35:09,660 --> 01:35:11,540
has stolen the Bifrost sword.

1493
01:35:11,870 --> 01:35:14,080
Tell us where it is...

1494
01:35:14,370 --> 01:35:16,880
or there will be consequences.

1495
01:35:20,710 --> 01:35:21,840
Bad ones.

1496
01:35:25,180 --> 01:35:26,180
Well?

1497
01:35:33,310 --> 01:35:34,310
You.

1498
01:36:10,560 --> 01:36:14,520
Well? Executioner?

1499
01:36:19,560 --> 01:36:20,770
Wait!

1500
01:36:20,860 --> 01:36:21,860
Wait!

1501
01:36:24,240 --> 01:36:25,400
I know where the sword is.

1502
01:37:08,660 --> 01:37:10,820
I never thought 
I'd be back here.

1503
01:37:14,490 --> 01:37:15,950
I thought it'd be a lot nicer.

1504
01:37:16,500 --> 01:37:17,960
I mean, not that it's not nice.

1505
01:37:18,040 --> 01:37:19,420
It's just, it's on fire.

1506
01:37:19,670 --> 01:37:20,920
Here, up here in the mountains.

1507
01:37:21,130 --> 01:37:23,210
Heat signatures. 
People clustered together.

1508
01:37:23,380 --> 01:37:24,380
She's coming for them.

1509
01:37:24,670 --> 01:37:25,710
Okay, drop me off at the palace

1510
01:37:25,760 --> 01:37:27,880
- and I'll draw her away. 
- And get yourself killed?

1511
01:37:28,090 --> 01:37:29,800
The people trapped down there 
are all that matters.

1512
01:37:29,840 --> 01:37:31,220
While I'm dealing with Hela, 
I need you two

1513
01:37:31,260 --> 01:37:32,550
to help get everyone off Asgard.

1514
01:37:32,800 --> 01:37:34,430
How the hell are we supposed 
to do that?

1515
01:37:35,100 --> 01:37:36,640
I have a man on the ground.

1516
01:37:42,520 --> 01:37:43,520
Asgard.

1517
01:37:47,150 --> 01:37:48,320
She's here.

1518
01:38:00,040 --> 01:38:01,620
Now the ship has a gun.

1519
01:38:01,870 --> 01:38:02,960
I'll take it from here.

1520
01:38:03,920 --> 01:38:06,800
I found this in the armory.

1521
01:38:10,170 --> 01:38:11,180
Good luck.

1522
01:38:12,890 --> 01:38:14,050
Your Majesty...

1523
01:38:16,140 --> 01:38:17,180
don't die.

1524
01:38:20,180 --> 01:38:21,810
You know what I mean.

1525
01:39:20,870 --> 01:39:22,620
We must keep moving!

1526
01:39:23,410 --> 01:39:25,000
Go to the Bifrost!

1527
01:40:07,790 --> 01:40:08,880
Sister.

1528
01:40:11,170 --> 01:40:12,800
You're still alive.

1529
01:40:13,090 --> 01:40:14,970
I love what you've done 
with the place.

1530
01:40:15,050 --> 01:40:16,380
Redecorating, I see.

1531
01:40:16,760 --> 01:40:18,800
It seems our father's solution

1532
01:40:18,890 --> 01:40:21,350
to every problem 
was to cover it up.

1533
01:40:22,970 --> 01:40:24,480
Or to cast it out.

1534
01:40:26,810 --> 01:40:30,230
He told you you were worthy. 
He said the same thing to me.

1535
01:40:30,940 --> 01:40:32,190
You see?

1536
01:40:32,940 --> 01:40:34,990
You never knew him.

1537
01:40:35,400 --> 01:40:37,160
Not at his best.

1538
01:40:37,450 --> 01:40:40,320
Odin and I drowned 
entire civilizations

1539
01:40:40,410 --> 01:40:41,910
in blood and tears.

1540
01:40:42,200 --> 01:40:44,100
Where do you think 
all this gold came from?

1541
01:40:45,290 --> 01:40:46,870
And then, one day...

1542
01:40:47,170 --> 01:40:50,040
he decided to become 
a benevolent king.

1543
01:40:50,380 --> 01:40:52,880
To foster peace, 
to protect life...

1544
01:40:54,130 --> 01:40:55,590
to have you.

1545
01:40:56,130 --> 01:40:58,430
I understand why you're angry.

1546
01:40:58,680 --> 01:41:00,140
And you are my sister, 
and technically

1547
01:41:00,220 --> 01:41:02,510
have a claim to the throne.

1548
01:41:02,760 --> 01:41:04,720
And believe me, I would love 
for someone else to rule.

1549
01:41:04,770 --> 01:41:05,890
But it can't be you.

1550
01:41:06,140 --> 01:41:09,650
You're just... 
The worst.

1551
01:41:11,310 --> 01:41:12,860
Okay, get up.

1552
01:41:13,230 --> 01:41:15,110
You're in my seat.

1553
01:41:16,280 --> 01:41:18,150
You know, Father once told me...

1554
01:41:18,400 --> 01:41:20,870
that a wise king 
never seeks out war.

1555
01:41:21,120 --> 01:41:23,530
But must always be ready for it.

1556
01:41:55,940 --> 01:41:57,190
Go back!

1557
01:42:02,370 --> 01:42:03,620
Go!

1558
01:42:38,780 --> 01:42:41,150
To be honest, I expected more.

1559
01:42:44,410 --> 01:42:45,410
Heimdall!

1560
01:42:47,740 --> 01:42:49,370
The sword!

1561
01:42:53,960 --> 01:42:55,420
Here's the difference 
between us.

1562
01:42:55,750 --> 01:42:57,210
I'm Odin's firstborn...

1563
01:42:57,460 --> 01:42:59,760
the rightful heir, 
the savior of Asgard.

1564
01:43:00,050 --> 01:43:01,760
And you're nothing.

1565
01:43:12,020 --> 01:43:14,810
So simple, 
even a blind man could see it.

1566
01:43:18,650 --> 01:43:20,780
Now you remind me of Dad.

1567
01:43:31,160 --> 01:43:32,830
The stupid dog won't die!

1568
01:43:54,940 --> 01:43:57,650
Everything's gonna be 
all right now. I got this.

1569
01:43:58,150 --> 01:44:00,110
You wanted to know who I am?

1570
01:44:01,190 --> 01:44:02,690
What the hell 
are you talking about?

1571
01:44:02,990 --> 01:44:04,280
You'll see!

1572
01:44:53,040 --> 01:44:55,160
You see? 
No one's going anywhere.

1573
01:44:55,450 --> 01:44:56,750
I'll get that sword...

1574
01:44:56,910 --> 01:44:59,540
even if I have to kill every 
single one of them to do it.

1575
01:45:26,360 --> 01:45:27,610
Hey, man.

1576
01:45:28,900 --> 01:45:30,160
I'm Korg. This is Miek.

1577
01:45:30,410 --> 01:45:31,570
We're gonna jump 
on that spaceship

1578
01:45:31,620 --> 01:45:32,870
and get out of here. 
Wanna come?

1579
01:45:42,330 --> 01:45:46,090
Your savior is here.

1580
01:45:53,720 --> 01:45:55,430
Did you miss me?

1581
01:45:55,770 --> 01:45:56,970
Everyone, on that ship now.

1582
01:46:01,520 --> 01:46:03,560
Welcome home. 
I saw you coming.

1583
01:46:03,860 --> 01:46:04,860
Of course you did.

1584
01:46:21,710 --> 01:46:23,790
It's a valiant effort, 
but you never stood a chance.

1585
01:46:24,960 --> 01:46:26,000
You see...

1586
01:46:26,880 --> 01:46:29,550
I'm not a queen or a monster.

1587
01:46:31,680 --> 01:46:33,220
I'm the Goddess of Death.

1588
01:46:34,470 --> 01:46:36,560
What were you the god of, again?

1589
01:46:48,190 --> 01:46:49,900
Even when you had two eyes...

1590
01:46:50,780 --> 01:46:52,490
you'd see only half the picture.

1591
01:46:54,030 --> 01:46:56,870
She's too strong. 
Without my hammer, I can't.

1592
01:46:58,240 --> 01:47:01,620
Are you Thor, 
the God of Hammers?

1593
01:47:04,880 --> 01:47:07,170
That hammer was to help you 
control your power,

1594
01:47:07,250 --> 01:47:08,500
to focus it.

1595
01:47:09,420 --> 01:47:11,010
It was never your source 
of strength.

1596
01:47:11,920 --> 01:47:14,050
It's too late. 
She's already taken Asgard.

1597
01:47:15,300 --> 01:47:17,850
Asgard is not a place. 
Never was.

1598
01:47:19,220 --> 01:47:20,310
This could be Asgard.

1599
01:47:21,680 --> 01:47:23,690
Asgard is where 
our people stand.

1600
01:47:24,690 --> 01:47:29,320
Even now, right now, 
those people need your help.

1601
01:47:37,160 --> 01:47:39,160
I'm not as strong as you.

1602
01:47:42,040 --> 01:47:43,040
No...

1603
01:47:44,460 --> 01:47:45,710
you're stronger.

1604
01:47:54,840 --> 01:47:56,090
Tell me, brother.

1605
01:47:56,180 --> 01:47:58,510
What were you the god of again?

1606
01:50:14,190 --> 01:50:16,230
- You're late. 
- You're missing an eye.

1607
01:50:16,570 --> 01:50:17,900
This isn't over.

1608
01:50:25,160 --> 01:50:26,790
I think we should 
disband the Revengers.

1609
01:50:28,450 --> 01:50:29,710
Hit her with a lightning blast.

1610
01:50:29,790 --> 01:50:30,960
I just hit her with 
the biggest lightning blast

1611
01:50:30,100 --> 01:50:32,120
in the history of lightning.

1612
01:50:32,210 --> 01:50:33,210
It did nothing.

1613
01:50:37,000 --> 01:50:39,510
We just need to hold her off 
until everyone's on board.

1614
01:50:40,300 --> 01:50:41,680
It won't end there.

1615
01:50:42,130 --> 01:50:45,390
The longer Hela's on Asgard, 
the more powerful she grows.

1616
01:50:45,720 --> 01:50:47,310
She'll hunt us down.

1617
01:50:47,510 --> 01:50:48,930
We need to stop her 
here and now.

1618
01:50:49,220 --> 01:50:50,270
So what do we do?

1619
01:50:51,270 --> 01:50:52,600
I'm not doing "Get Help."

1620
01:51:04,990 --> 01:51:08,120
Asgard's not a place, 
it's a people.

1621
01:51:10,160 --> 01:51:11,160
Loki...

1622
01:51:11,500 --> 01:51:13,330
this was never about 
stopping Ragnarok.

1623
01:51:13,670 --> 01:51:15,540
This was about causing Ragnarok.

1624
01:51:15,750 --> 01:51:17,250
Surtur's crown, the vault.

1625
01:51:19,130 --> 01:51:20,340
It's the only way.

1626
01:51:21,050 --> 01:51:22,380
Bold move, brother.

1627
01:51:23,800 --> 01:51:25,140
Even for me.

1628
01:51:28,430 --> 01:51:29,430
Shall we?

1629
01:51:30,600 --> 01:51:31,600
After you.

1630
01:51:57,290 --> 01:51:58,630
This is madness.

1631
01:52:12,180 --> 01:52:13,680
Go! Go, now!

1632
01:53:14,950 --> 01:53:16,250
For Asgard.

1633
01:53:30,680 --> 01:53:31,890
Hela!

1634
01:53:56,620 --> 01:54:00,620
With the Eternal Flame, 
you are reborn.

1635
01:54:11,890 --> 01:54:13,390
Hela, enough!

1636
01:54:17,220 --> 01:54:19,850
You want Asgard, it's yours.

1637
01:54:20,350 --> 01:54:23,560
Whatever game you're playing, 
it won't work.

1638
01:54:23,810 --> 01:54:25,230
You can't defeat me.

1639
01:54:26,110 --> 01:54:27,360
No, I know.

1640
01:54:29,070 --> 01:54:30,070
But he can.

1641
01:54:34,580 --> 01:54:35,660
No.

1642
01:54:43,750 --> 01:54:47,050
Tremble before me, Asgard!

1643
01:54:47,300 --> 01:54:49,420
I am your reckoning!

1644
01:54:58,930 --> 01:55:00,350
The people are safe.

1645
01:55:01,100 --> 01:55:02,770
That's all that matters.

1646
01:55:04,690 --> 01:55:05,900
We're fulfilling the prophecy.

1647
01:55:06,650 --> 01:55:07,900
I hate this prophecy.

1648
01:55:08,190 --> 01:55:09,860
So do I, but we have no choice.

1649
01:55:10,150 --> 01:55:11,820
Surtur destroys Asgard...

1650
01:55:12,110 --> 01:55:14,320
he destroys Hela, 
so that our people may live.

1651
01:55:14,450 --> 01:55:16,030
But we need to let him 
finish the job,

1652
01:55:16,120 --> 01:55:17,200
otherwise...

1653
01:55:18,950 --> 01:55:19,950
No!

1654
01:55:22,460 --> 01:55:24,290
Hulk, stop, you moron!

1655
01:55:33,510 --> 01:55:34,550
Hulk, stop.

1656
01:55:34,800 --> 01:55:37,640
Just for once in your life, 
don't smash.

1657
01:55:39,010 --> 01:55:40,600
Big monster!

1658
01:55:41,060 --> 01:55:42,140
Let's go!

1659
01:55:44,020 --> 01:55:45,020
Fine.

1660
01:56:09,210 --> 01:56:11,880
I am Asgard's doom!

1661
01:56:53,380 --> 01:56:55,170
What have I done?

1662
01:56:56,470 --> 01:56:58,760
You saved us from extinction.

1663
01:56:59,050 --> 01:57:00,640
Asgard is not a place...

1664
01:57:02,430 --> 01:57:03,970
it's a people.

1665
01:57:33,300 --> 01:57:34,710
It suits you.

1666
01:57:37,590 --> 01:57:39,930
Maybe you're not so bad 
after all, brother.

1667
01:57:40,390 --> 01:57:41,430
Maybe not.

1668
01:57:42,890 --> 01:57:43,930
Thank you.

1669
01:57:44,850 --> 01:57:47,020
If you were here, 
I might even give you a hug.

1670
01:57:51,520 --> 01:57:52,690
I'm here.

1671
01:58:16,920 --> 01:58:18,170
Your throne.

1672
01:58:33,480 --> 01:58:36,400
So. King of Asgard.

1673
01:58:47,080 --> 01:58:48,080
Where to?

1674
01:58:49,330 --> 01:58:50,580
I'm not sure.

1675
01:58:51,330 --> 01:58:52,420
Any suggestions?

1676
01:58:55,290 --> 01:58:57,000
Miek, where are you from?

1677
01:58:57,380 --> 01:58:59,170
Miek's dead.

1678
01:58:59,460 --> 01:59:02,470
Yeah, no, I accidentally 
stomped on him on the bridge.

1679
01:59:02,630 --> 01:59:03,970
I've just felt so guilty,

1680
01:59:04,050 --> 01:59:05,510
I've been carrying him around 
all day.

1681
01:59:07,390 --> 01:59:09,310
Miek, you're alive!

1682
01:59:09,390 --> 01:59:10,560
He's alive, guys.

1683
01:59:10,640 --> 01:59:11,980
What was 
your question again, bro?

1684
01:59:13,650 --> 01:59:14,650
Earth it is.

1685
02:01:31,410 --> 02:01:32,830
Do you really think 
it's a good idea

1686
02:01:32,910 --> 02:01:33,990
to go back to Earth?

1687
02:01:34,580 --> 02:01:35,580
Yes, of course.

1688
02:01:35,660 --> 02:01:37,750
The people of Earth love me. 
I'm very popular.

1689
02:01:38,290 --> 02:01:40,080
Let me rephrase that.

1690
02:01:40,460 --> 02:01:42,250
Do you really think 
it's a good idea

1691
02:01:42,340 --> 02:01:43,710
to bring me back to Earth?

1692
02:01:44,380 --> 02:01:46,340
Probably not, to be honest.

1693
02:01:46,420 --> 02:01:48,130
I wouldn't worry, brother.

1694
02:01:48,220 --> 02:01:51,220
I feel like everything's 
gonna work out fine.

1695
02:08:20,320 --> 02:08:21,320
Boy.

1696
02:08:29,700 --> 02:08:33,700
I just gotta say, 
I'm proud of you all.

1697
02:08:34,120 --> 02:08:37,330
This revolution has been 
a huge success. Yay, us!

1698
02:08:37,710 --> 02:08:40,090
Pat on the back. 
Pat on the back.

1699
02:08:40,170 --> 02:08:42,420
Come on. No?

1700
02:08:42,960 --> 02:08:44,970
Me too. 'Cause I've been 
a big part of it.

1701
02:08:45,050 --> 02:08:47,840
Can't have a revolution 
without somebody to overthrow.

1702
02:08:47,930 --> 02:08:49,800
So, you're welcome.

1703
02:08:50,100 --> 02:08:52,350
And, it's a tie.
